#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cepa-until — runs the repo's queue for a time window, unattended.

## Why it exists

The three batch executors of the harness (`/board-flow:drain`, `/common:drain-plan`,
`/board-flow:prove-drain`) are limited by COUNT: `--max N`. A count is the
wrong shape for using idle time — you don't know how many items fit in a
night, you know how many hours you have. What is missing is a clock ceiling.

But a clock alone doesn't solve it, because what kills a long session is not
time: it is CONTEXT. A 12h session blows up long before the 12h mark, and
whoever resumes it today is a person typing `/common:autonomous-resume` — at 3am,
nobody types.

Hence the design: **one item per subprocess**. This supervisor fires

    claude -p "/common:drain-plan <queue> --max 1"

once per item, in a fresh process every time. Context overflow stops being a
failure and becomes the normal end of a subprocess — the supervisor fires the
next one, with a clean context window. That, and only that, is what makes 12h
possible.

## What it deliberately does NOT do

It doesn't reserve an item, doesn't record an outcome, doesn't know the topology
and doesn't know what a card is. Whoever does all of that is `/common:drain-plan` + `cepa-plan`,
which already have the needed state machine, built and tested:

  - `cepa-plan start` reserves the item by SIGNING the reservation (session, pid, host);
  - `cepa-plan queue` returns as executable the reservation whose pid died — the
    "orphan reservation". It is what keeps a dead subprocess from locking the queue
    forever, and it is exactly the guarantee a supervisor needs;
  - `cepa-plan finish` records the outcome, including the route that only the human closes.

This file is the wiring around that: clock, circuit breaker and log.

## The owner's four decisions (2026-08-30)

1. **The source is the on-disk queue** (`/common:drain-plan`), not the board column.
   The queue keeps the ORDER and the WHY, and doesn't depend on Jira being up at 3am.
2. **Circuit breaker at 3 failures in a row.** Below that it's bad luck; above it is
   burning the whole window on a systemic problem.
3. **One commit per item, on a single branch.** No merge train and no N branches
   dangling waiting for someone to notice — which is the measured defect of Maestro in
   wave 1 of WEGO-parallel (5 green branches sitting idle, 2 of them for half a day).
   This is a GUARD, not an intention: the starting branch is recorded and checked between
   items, and the run ends if it changed. The supervisor neither commits nor creates
   a branch — the flow inside the subprocess does that —, so without the
   check the night could scatter into silent branches and the banner
   would keep printing the right branch. (Gap found by the acceptance gate,
   2026-08-30.)
   **Revision of 2026-09-24: the night branch belongs to the supervisor.** The check
   above looked at the main clone's branch, and the 09/23 run on WEGO showed
   that this is not enough: each subprocess opened its own worktree from
   `origin/main` (`session/wego2308`, `session/wego2309`...), the main clone
   stayed on `main` all night and the guard never fired. Nothing merged, and 20
   of the 25 rounds stalled because the previous card only existed on a
   loose branch. Now the supervisor creates the `until/<run>` worktree at launch, runs
   each subprocess INSIDE it (`/common:drain-plan ... --na-branch
   until/<run>`), and each card starts from where the previous one ended. Nothing goes
   to `main` or to `origin`: in the morning the owner merges a single branch.

   **And the full build is also the supervisor's.** In the same run, 2308 closed
   `done` with `clean verify` run BEFORE a last refactor, and the
   `validation-lead` (the phase that runs the full build at the end of the card) did not
   run in any of the 5 cards. After each `done` item, the supervisor runs
   the full build on the night branch. If red, the item's commits go to
   `until/<run>-vermelho-<id>`, the night branch goes back to where it was and the
   item becomes `blocked` with the reason. The next card never starts on code
   that didn't pass.

4. **`--dangerously-skip-permissions` on.** Without it the subprocess hangs on the
   first permission prompt and the night dies in silence. It is explicit in the
   banner and can be turned off with `--with-permissions`.

## Where the cut happens

Between items, NEVER in the middle of one. Killing an item halfway leaves a dirty tree and a
dangling reservation. Two margins control this:

  - `--min-reserve` (default 45min): does not START an item if less than
    that is left. An item that doesn't fit in the window is work thrown away.
  - `--slack` (default 60min): how far an item ALREADY RUNNING may go past the deadline
    before being killed. Past that, it is a death by timeout — recorded, and the
    orphan reservation goes back to the queue on the next run.

## The account usage ceiling (5h)

The Claude account has a quota per 5h window. On 2026-09-17 the queue hit the
ceiling at 01:00 with reset at 3:20 and the window lasting until 06:17: the run stopped and ~3h of window
went unused, and the in-flight item lost what it had already done. Two rules:

  - **Wait for the reset (when it hits).** With the reset time known and
    fitting in the window, the supervisor sleeps until reset + `CEPA_UNTIL_MARGEM_RESET`
    (default 120s) and resumes the SAME item. The cut attempt doesn't count toward the
    item's attempt ceiling nor toward the circuit breaker. Three cuts in a row with no progress
    between them end the run: the announced reset is not lifting the ceiling.
  - **Don't start an item with the quota running out.** Each subprocess runs with
    `--output-format stream-json`, which carries the `rate_limit_event` event with the
    5h window usage (`unifiedWindows.five_hour.utilization`, a 0–1 fraction) and
    the reset in epoch. Before each item the supervisor projects the usage: the last
    reading, plus the largest item cost measured in this window (difference between the
    start readings of two consecutive items). If the next item doesn't fit
    (projection > 100%), or if with no history the reading is already past 90%, it waits for the
    reset before starting — the wait costs little and avoids the cut.
  - **If the reset doesn't fit in the window, start anyway.** An item cut
    midway doesn't lose its work: its worktree stays on disk with what was already
    done and the next run's `start` claims the orphan reservation and resumes
    from there (WEGO-2293, cut at 30min on 2026-09-18, closed in the next
    run in 1h05). The next run is born from the clone's HEAD, so the
    commits the item left on the previous night branch only reach it
    through INHERITANCE: at launch, the branch that holds commits of an item still
    open in the queue, and that the clone doesn't have, is merged into the new branch (on
    09/27 WEGO-2283 restarted from zero with 15 commits parked in
    `until/2026-09-27-1632`). A merge with conflict refuses the launch. Stopping, on the other hand,
    leaves the whole window unused: on 2026-09-18 the
    supervisor stopped at 19:45 with 24% of quota and 1h35 of window left.
    Half an item is worth more than zero — the supervisor warns that the item
    will probably be cut, records `cota_apertada` and carries on.

If the ceiling was hit in the middle of an item and the wait for the reset doesn't fit in the window,
the run stops (reason `limite-de-uso`): the item stays where it was.

## Network drop

On 2026-09-18 the internet went down at 11:32 in the middle of WEGO-2293: `claude` retried
10 times, exited 1 with "Can't reach the API server (ENOTFOUND)", and the next two
attempts died the same way in 3 minutes each. The supervisor
read three "no progress", marked the item `blocked` and shut down via the circuit breaker —
over a drop that was neither the item's nor the account's. The rule:

  - **Wait for the network to come back.** When the final `result` of the stream-json comes with
    `terminal_reason: api_error` and the message is a network one (ENOTFOUND,
    ECONNREFUSED, "Can't reach the API server"...), the attempt doesn't count toward the
    item's ceiling nor toward the circuit breaker. The supervisor probes `CEPA_UNTIL_SONDA_REDE`
    (default `api.anthropic.com:443`) every `CEPA_UNTIL_SONDA_INTERVALO`
    seconds (default 60) until the network is back, and resumes the SAME item — its
    reservation becomes orphan and `start` claims it. The wait goes at most
    up to the deadline minus the minimum reserve; past that, the run stops with reason
    `sem-rede`. Three drops in a row with no progress between them also stop the
    run: the probe says the network is back, but `claude` still can't reach the
    API, and insisting repeats the night.

## When it stops

It stops at the first of: deadline reached, queue with no executable item (the reason comes from
`cepa-plan queue` — `fim-da-fila`, `bloqueado`, `bloqueado-antes`), circuit breaker,
or account usage ceiling whose wait doesn't fit in the window.
An item that comes out `blocked` STOPS the batch — a `cepa-plan` rule, inherited from
`/board-flow:drain`: re-running measures the same stall.

## Signals

On 2026-09-28 WEGO's run 2003 died silently: the `.jsonl` stopped at
`item_start`, the card closed `done` on its own and the full build never ran. The
hypothesis left standing was the closed terminal tab: SIGHUP goes to the terminal's
group, `claude` runs in its own session and survives, the supervisor doesn't.

  - **SIGHUP is ignored**, and screen output now tolerates the vanished
    terminal (without that, the next `print` kills the run with EIO).
  - **SIGTERM and Ctrl+C** record `run_interrompido` in the `.jsonl` (signal, in-flight
    item, phase and child pid) and leave `<run>.estado.json` as
    `interrompido`.
  - `run_start` and the state record the supervisor's **pid and host**. The
    `cepa-until pendentes` (and through it `cepa-doctor` and
    `/common:until-review`) points at the `rodando` run whose pid died, and at the
    `interrompido` one, with the full build that was missed.
  - **SIGTERM and Ctrl+C end the child** (the `claude` or build group):
    going on by itself, it would change the card with nobody to run the build
    afterwards. Dead, the reservation becomes orphan and the next run resumes the item.
  - `cepa-until fecha-morto <queue>/<run> --yes` runs the missed build and,
    if green, closes the record and leaves the run ready for `aterrissar`.

## Hook that only counts after reinstalling

Hooks run from the plugin installed in the cache, a copy of the clone at the last
install, and not from the night branch. In run 2026-09-28-1146 two items
fixed hooks and the next 4 rounds were still blocked by the old versions,
with nothing in the run saying so. Now, when the night branch changes a
file under `<plugin>/hooks/` (a folder with `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`), the screen
warns right after the item, the record gains `hook_so_apos_reinstalar`, and the end
asks for `reinstalar-plugin` under "Fica com você": it takes effect after `aterrissar` and
`bin/install.sh`.

## After the end

With the run over, a final `claude -p "/common:until-review <run>"` reads the
record and the subprocesses' output and writes `<run>.review.md` next to them: what
the owner needs to do, in closed questions. It doesn't run when the run stopped on
the quota (the analysis would hit the same ceiling) nor with `--no-analysis`; in both
cases the command is run by hand afterwards.

Usage:
    cepa-until my-queue --for 12h
    cepa-until my-queue --until 07:00
    cepa-until my-queue --for 3h --dry-run     # the run's plan, without executing
    cepa-until fecha-morto my-queue/<run> --yes  # closes a dead supervisor's run
"""

import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import signal
import socket
import select
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timedelta
from pathlib import Path

try:
    import yaml
except ImportError:
    print("cepa-until precisa de PyYAML (pip install pyyaml)", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / "hooks"))
import _queuepath as qp  # noqa: E402  (the queue lives in two layouts during the transition)
import _ownertext  # noqa: E402  (the human section of a blocked item)
import _clihelp  # noqa: E402
import _dirt  # noqa: E402  (single definition of "dirty clone")

CEPA_PLAN = HERE / "cepa-plan"
CEPA_UNTIL_DIGEST = HERE / "cepa-until-digest"

# Where the night worktree is born. Same home and same variable as
# `cepa` (the launcher): outside the tree synced by Insync.
ENV_WORKTREE_HOME = "CEPA_WORKTREE_HOME"

# The full build the supervisor runs after each `done` item, chosen by the
# file the repo has. A repo with none of them must state the command
# (`--verify`) or waive it (`--no-verify`, or a committed `.claude/no-build`
# without `tests/run-all.sh`): a night without a full build is the hole that 2308
# exposed.
VERIFY_BY_FILE = [
    ("mvnw", "./mvnw -B clean verify"),
    ("gradlew", "./gradlew build"),
    ("tests/run-all.sh", "tests/run-all.sh"),
]

# The suite of a repo that compiles nothing (cepa itself). `.claude/no-build`
# waives the `gate-advance` baseline because there is no build; it doesn't mean
# there is no suite. With both in the repo, the suite runs: in run 2026-09-26-2203
# `no-build` alone let 18 items close without anyone running the whole suite.
SUITE_WITHOUT_BUILD = "tests/run-all.sh"


# JavaScript repo: `package.json` names the build and the suite through its
# `scripts`, and the lock file names the package manager. The command starts
# with the install because the night worktree is born without `node_modules`:
# on wego-digitacao-demo, 2026-10-24, `npm run build` in a fresh worktree failed
# with `next: command not found`. A frozen-lockfile install also fails when the
# lock fell behind.
JS_BY_LOCK = [
    ("pnpm-lock.yaml", "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile", "pnpm"),
    ("yarn.lock", "yarn install --frozen-lockfile", "yarn"),
    ("package-lock.json", "npm ci", "npm"),
]
JS_WITHOUT_LOCK = ("npm install", "npm")
# The `test` that `npm init` writes is not a suite: it only fails.
JS_FAKE_TEST = "no test specified"


def javascript_verify(repo):
    """(command, origin) from the root `package.json`, or None if it has neither
    `build` nor a real `test` (then the repo still has no known build)."""
    pj = repo / "package.json"
    if not pj.exists():
        return None
    try:
        scripts = json.loads(pj.read_text()).get("scripts") or {}
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(scripts, dict):
        return None
    has_build = bool(scripts.get("build"))
    test = scripts.get("test") or ""
    has_test = bool(test) and JS_FAKE_TEST not in test
    if not (has_build or has_test):
        return None
    install, pm, lock = None, None, None
    for file_name, cmd, manager in JS_BY_LOCK:
        if (repo / file_name).exists():
            install, pm, lock = cmd, manager, file_name
            break
    if install is None:
        install, pm = JS_WITHOUT_LOCK
    steps = [install]
    if has_build:
        steps.append(f"{pm} run build")
    if has_test:
        steps.append(f"{pm} test")
    scripts_seen = " e ".join(n for n, t in (("build", has_build),
                                             ("test", has_test)) if t)
    origin = (f"achei `package.json` com {scripts_seen}"
              + (f" e `{lock}`" if lock else ", sem arquivo de lock"))
    return " && ".join(steps), origin

# The end-of-run questions are asked on a terminal, but the owner is usually
# not there when an overnight run ends (PID 84993, run WEGO 2026-10-07-2132,
# stayed alive 15 days blocked in `input()`). After this wait (seconds) with no
# keystroke the run prints the `cepa-until decide` command and exits.
ANSWER_WAIT_SEC = float(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_ESPERA_RESPOSTA", "600"))

# How long the end-of-run analysis may take. It reads a summary of tens of KB,
# not the whole `.log`; 20 minutes is slack, not an estimate.
ANALYSIS_LIMIT_SEC = int(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_LIMITE_ANALISE", "1200"))

# 45min and not 25: in run 2026-09-27-1632 of wego-acessos-backend, 3 of the 4
# delivered items went past 25min (1610 s, 2127 s, 2700 s) and WEGO-2283 started with
# 35min to spare, ran 95min and went 1h past the deadline before being killed by the slack.
DEFAULT_MIN_RESERVE = "45m"
DEFAULT_SLACK = "60m"
DEFAULT_MAX_FAILURES = 3

# How long to wait between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when killing an item that blew
# through the slack. The polite SIGTERM is the first request; SIGKILL exists because a
# process may IGNORE the first (build with a trap, shell wrapper), and without the
# escalation it would keep running all night while the supervisor believed
# it had killed it. Adjustable only so the test can exercise the escalation without
# waiting half a minute per case.
SIGTERM_GRACE = float(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_GRACA_SIGTERM", "30"))

# Statuses that count as PROGRESS on the item. `dropped` is included because the item left
# the queue by a recorded decision, not because the run failed.
TERMINAL_STATES = {"done", "blocked", "dropped"}

# `blocked` items IN A ROW that end the run. `blocked` is progress (the item
# left the queue with a reason), so the circuit breaker never sees them — and a queue that stalls
# item after item on the same outside cause burns the window rediscovering the cause.
# On 2026-09-23 that was 20 rounds and US$ 14.30; on 2026-09-15, 7 in a row in
# 11 minutes. It is not the item's failure: it is the queue being stalled, and the run stops with its
# own reason (`fila-travada`) instead of `disjuntor`.
DEFAULT_MAX_BLOCKED = 3

# How many subprocesses the SAME window spends on the SAME item before taking it out of
# the way. `queue` always hands out the first executable item, and a dead subprocess
# returns the reservation as an orphan — so an item that doesn't move would be
# re-offered forever. On 2026-08-30 WEGO-1941 consumed 3 of the run's 5
# attempts with 15 pending behind it. Two is the ceiling because the second
# attempt has measured value: WEGO-2206 failed stuck on a background build
# and closed on the retry, when the build had already finished.
DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS_PER_ITEM = 2

# How many red returns an item withstands before going to `blocked`
# (Revision 3 of until-fim-sem-dono). A return is an item that closed `done`,
# went red on two full builds in a row and went back to `pending` with
# the note. On the second one, the agent already had the side branch and the reason in hand and didn't
# solve it: repeating again burns the window on the same card.
MAX_RED_RETURNS = 2

# What `claude` prints when the ACCOUNT hit the usage ceiling — not the item, not
# the queue, not the topology. Without recognizing this the supervisor reads only "exited 1 and the
# item didn't move" and blames the card: on 2026-08-30 two attempts of 92s and 4s
# went into the circuit breaker as if WEGO-1941 were systematically bad, and the
# morning report sent the owner to investigate the wrong item. Retrying doesn't
# lift the ceiling either — the clock does —, so the run waits for the reset (or
# stops, with its own reason, if the wait doesn't fit) instead of knocking on the same door.
USAGE_LIMIT = re.compile(
    r"(?:you'?ve|you have)\s+(?:hit|reached)\s+your\s+[\w\s-]{0,24}\blimit\b"
    r"|\busage limit reached\b"
    r"|\blimit reached\b\s*[\u00b7\u2022\u2219|-]\s*resets\b",
    re.I)

# The reset time, when the message carries it — it is the datum that decides whether to reschedule the
# window or give up the night, and it is lost if the supervisor only records "hit the limit".
LIMIT_RESET = re.compile(r"resets?(?:\s+at)?\s+([^\n(\"]{1,40})", re.I)

# The same time, in a form that becomes a clock: "3:20am", "8pm", with the optional
# timezone in parentheses. A reset with a date in front ("Sep 22, 4pm") deliberately does NOT
# match: it is the weekly ceiling, which fits in no window, and guessing
# the wrong day would make the supervisor sleep until a meaningless hour.
RESET_HOUR = re.compile(
    r"resets?(?:\s+at)?\s+(\d{1,2})(?::(\d{2}))?\s*([ap])\.?m\.?"
    r"(?:\s*\(([^)]+)\))?", re.I)

# Margin after the announced reset before resuming. The server's clock and ours
# don't match to the second, and waking up too early burns an attempt on the ceiling.
# Adjustable only so the test can exercise the wait without sleeping minutes.
RESET_MARGIN = float(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_MARGEM_RESET", "120"))

# Consecutive cuts by the ceiling, with no progress between them, that end the run. The
# announced reset is not lifting the ceiling — waiting again repeats the night.
MAX_CONSECUTIVE_WAITS = 3

# With no item cost measured yet, the reading from which the supervisor won't
# risk starting a new item in the same 5h window.
QUOTA_WITHOUT_HISTORY = 0.9

# The mark of "you are inside an unattended window", exported to each
# subprocess. The `no-background-build` hook only exists when it is in the
# environment: in an interactive session sending the build to the background is the
# right thing (the notification re-invokes the session), and under `claude -p` it means losing the
# item, because there is no next turn to collect the result.
ENV_WINDOW = "CEPA_UNTIL_RUN"

# The ceiling `claude -p` uses to wait for background work before
# killing itself. The default (10 min) killed WEGO-2224 at 47 minutes with the 3 Tasks
# merged and the test phase still to do: `Background tasks still running after
# 600s; terminating`, exit 0, and the main clone parked on an
# integration branch — which the next item's branch check read as a branch switch
# and ended the window with 6h54 to spare (run of 2026-09-03).
#
# `0` is the value the harness's own message indicates for waiting without a ceiling.
# Waiting without a ceiling is safe here because the REAL ceiling is this supervisor's clock:
# `--limite-item` kills the subprocess and `--slack` kills the item that goes past
# the deadline. We swapped a blind 10-min cut for a cut that knows the window.
#
# This is only safe together with `no-background-build`, which blocks in the same window
# the background work that NEVER ends on its own (a watcher with `while true`,
# `persistent: true`): without it, waiting without a ceiling would swap the 10-min cut for the
# whole item's limit. The two form a pair — don't touch one without the other.
#
# A value already set in the environment by the operator wins: whoever chose it explicitly
# knows what they want.
#
# MEASURED ON 09/27/2026 (claude 2.1.283): the wait doesn't happen. With the variable
# at 0, absent or 120000, a `claude -p` that left `bash build.sh` in the background
# exited in ~15s and the build died with it; an armed `Monitor` doesn't
# hold the turn either. What collects a build longer than 10 min today is the recipe that
# `no-background-build` teaches: write `EXIT=` to a file and wait for it in the
# foreground. The export stays because it costs nothing and the behavior
# may come back in a future version; don't count on it.
ENV_BG_WAIT = "CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS"

# How much of the subprocess output the limit recognizer looks at. Reading the final piece
# of THIS attempt (and not the whole log, which is append-only) is what keeps us from
# reacting to the message of an earlier attempt; reading only the tail is what keeps us from
# reacting to the report of an agent that MENTIONS usage limits in prose.
OUTPUT_TAIL = 2000

# What `claude` writes in the final `result` when it died for lack of NETWORK
# (copied from the run of 2026-09-18). Only counts together with `terminal_reason:
# api_error`: an agent that MENTIONS ENOTFOUND in prose is not a network drop.
NO_NETWORK = re.compile(
    r"can'?t reach the api server"
    r"|\b(?:ENOTFOUND|ECONNREFUSED|ECONNRESET|ETIMEDOUT|EAI_AGAIN|EHOSTUNREACH"
    r"|ENETUNREACH)\b"
    r"|\bfetch failed\b", re.I)

# Where the supervisor knocks to find out whether the network is back (host:port, TCP), and how
# often. The API is the right target: it is what `claude` needs to reach.
NETWORK_PROBE = os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_SONDA_REDE", "api.anthropic.com:443")
PROBE_INTERVAL = float(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_SONDA_INTERVALO", "60"))

# Consecutive network drops, with no progress between them, that end the run: the
# probe sees the network, `claude` doesn't — waiting again doesn't change that.
MAX_CONSECUTIVE_DROPS = 3


# ── clock ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

_DUR = re.compile(r"^(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\s*([hm])$", re.I)


# A `rodando` run whose state has no pid (recorded before 2026-09-29): with no way to
# ask the system whether the supervisor is alive, the death signal is the deadline having
# passed more than this ago. It covers the default slack (60min), the last item's
# full build and the end-of-run analysis.
MARGIN_WITHOUT_PID = timedelta(hours=3)


class TolerantOutput:
    """stdout/stderr that survive a closed terminal.

    Ignoring SIGHUP (the closed tab) is not enough: the terminal vanishes with it, and the
    supervisor's next `print` blows up with `OSError` (EIO) and kills it just the same,
    only one step later. On the first write that fails, the descriptor
    is repointed to /dev/null and the run goes on; the `.jsonl` record and the
    `.log`, which are files, keep recording everything."""

    def __init__(self, stream):
        self._stream = stream

    def _discard(self):
        try:
            null_fd = os.open(os.devnull, os.O_WRONLY)
            os.dup2(null_fd, self._stream.fileno())
            os.close(null_fd)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass

    def write(self, text):
        try:
            return self._stream.write(text)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self._discard()
            try:
                return self._stream.write(text)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                return len(text)

    def flush(self):
        try:
            self._stream.flush()
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self._discard()

    def __getattr__(self, name):
        return getattr(self._stream, name)


def parse_duration(text, flag="--for"):
    """'12h' / '90m' → timedelta. Without a unit it doesn't pass: '12' is ambiguous and the
    ambiguity here costs a whole night in the wrong unit.

    `flag` exists because three options go through here (--for, --min-reserve,
    --slack) and a refusal that names the wrong flag sends you to check the
    wrong argument — which a perturbation caught on 2026-08-30.
    """
    m = _DUR.match(text.strip())
    if not m:
        raise ValueError(
            f"{flag} {text!r} não é uma duração: use '12h' ou '90m' (a unidade "
            "é obrigatória)")
    value, unit = float(m.group(1)), m.group(2).lower()
    if value <= 0:
        raise ValueError(f"{flag} {text!r} não é positivo")
    return timedelta(hours=value) if unit == "h" else timedelta(minutes=value)


def parse_until(text, now):
    """'07:00' → the next 07:00 in the future. If it already passed today, it is tomorrow."""
    try:
        hh, mm = text.strip().split(":")
        target = now.replace(hour=int(hh), minute=int(mm), second=0, microsecond=0)
    except Exception:
        raise ValueError(f"--until {text!r} não é um horário: use 'HH:MM'")
    if target <= now:
        target += timedelta(days=1)
    return target


def human(td):
    total = int(max(td.total_seconds(), 0))
    h, m = total // 3600, (total % 3600) // 60
    return f"{h}h{m:02d}" if h else f"{m}min"


# ── screen: color, bar and truncation, only when the output is a terminal ──
#
# The run's output is a record that scrolls for hours: in a terminal tab, in a
# `nohup` or in a file. The decoration (color, glyphs, window bar and the line
# that redraws itself while `claude` runs) exists only in the first case. Outside
# a terminal, or with NO_COLOR, the output is byte for byte the old one: it is what the
# tests read and what a `nohup`'s `.log` keeps. `CEPA_UNTIL_COR=sempre`
# and `CEPA_UNTIL_COR=nunca` force it.

class Screen:
    COLORS = {"verde": "\033[32m", "vermelho": "\033[31m", "amarelo": "\033[33m",
             "ciano": "\033[36m", "magenta": "\033[35m", "cinza": "\033[2m",
             "negrito": "\033[1m"}
    RESET = "\033[0m"

    def __init__(self, stream=None):
        stream = sys.stdout if stream is None else stream
        mode = os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_COR", "").strip().lower()
        if mode in ("sempre", "always", "1"):
            enabled = True
        elif mode in ("nunca", "never", "0") or os.environ.get("NO_COLOR"):
            enabled = False
        else:
            try:
                enabled = bool(stream.isatty()) and os.environ.get("TERM") != "dumb"
            except (AttributeError, ValueError):
                enabled = False
        self.enabled = enabled
        self.full_title = False

    def width(self):
        try:
            return min(shutil.get_terminal_size((100, 40)).columns, 120)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return 100

    def c(self, color, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            return text
        return f"{self.COLORS[color]}{text}{self.RESET}"

    def truncate(self, text, slack=0):
        """Truncates to the terminal width, with an ellipsis. Outside a terminal,
        or with --full-title, returns it whole."""
        if not self.enabled or self.full_title:
            return text
        n = max(self.width() - slack, 20)
        return text if len(text) <= n else text[: n - 1] + "…"

    def bar(self, frac, n=16, color="ciano"):
        k = round(max(0.0, min(1.0, frac)) * n)
        return self.c(color, "▰" * k) + self.c("cinza", "▱" * (n - k))

    def rule(self, title):
        """`── title ─────`. Outside a terminal it is just `── title`, the text that
        the tests and the `digest` look for."""
        if not self.enabled:
            return f"── {title}"
        rest = max(0, self.width() - len(title) - 4)
        return (self.c("magenta", "── ") + self.c("negrito", title) + " "
                + self.c("magenta", "─" * rest))

    def stamp(self, when=None):
        return self.c("cinza", f"[{(when or datetime.now()).strftime('%H:%M')}]")

    def clear_line(self):
        if self.enabled:
            sys.stdout.write("\r\033[2K")
            sys.stdout.flush()


SCREEN = Screen()

# What goes in front of each step of an item, judging by what the text says. Outside
# a terminal it is always the old `→`.
_STEPS = [
    (r"^verde na 2ª", "↻", "amarelo"),
    (r"^(verde|done)\b", "✓", "verde"),
    (r"^vermelho \(", "↻", "amarelo"),
    (r"^(VERMELHO|SEM PROGRESSO|SEM REDE|LIMITE DE USO|`done` sem|\d+ tentativa)",
     "✗", "vermelho"),
    (r"^(blocked|`blocked`|dropped)", "⊘", "vermelho"),
    (r"^(sondo|espero)", "⏳", "amarelo"),
    (r"^o item deixou arquivos", "⚠", "amarelo"),
    (r"^build completo:", "▸", "cinza"),
]


OUTCOME_GLYPHS = {
    "entregue": ("✓", "verde"), "rota-humana": ("◐", "amarelo"),
    "em-andamento": ("…", "amarelo"), "volta-vermelha": ("↻", "amarelo"),
    "travado": ("✗", "vermelho"), "sem-progresso": ("✗", "vermelho"),
    "done-sem-commit": ("✗", "vermelho"), "dropped": ("⊘", "vermelho"),
    "sem-rede": ("⚡", "amarelo"), "limite-de-uso": ("⚡", "amarelo"),
}


def step(text):
    """One outcome line inside an item's block."""
    if not SCREEN.enabled:
        print(f"          → {text}")
        return
    glyph, color = "→", "cinza"
    for default_value, g, c in _STEPS:
        if re.match(default_value, text):
            glyph, color = g, c
            break
    if "rota humana" in text and color == "verde":
        glyph, color = "◐", "amarelo"
    head_, _, rest = text.partition(" (")
    if rest:
        rest = SCREEN.c("cinza", " (" + rest)
    print("       " + SCREEN.c(color, f"{glyph} {head_}") + rest)


def wait_for_child(proc, limit_sec, label):
    """Waits for the subprocess up to `limit_sec`. Returns True if it finished, False
    if it overran. On a terminal, redraws every 30s a line with the elapsed
    time: without it the supervisor goes mute for up to an hour inside the item."""
    start = time.monotonic()
    limit = max(limit_sec, 1)
    last_item = -LIVE_LINE_INTERVAL
    while True:
        spent = time.monotonic() - start
        if SCREEN.enabled and spent - last_item >= LIVE_LINE_INTERVAL:
            last_item = spent
            sys.stdout.write(
                "\r\033[2K       " + SCREEN.c("amarelo", f"▶ {label} rodando")
                + SCREEN.c("cinza", f"  {int(spent)}s  " if spent < 60 else
                         f"  {human(timedelta(seconds=spent))}  ")
                + SCREEN.bar(spent / limit, color="amarelo")
                + SCREEN.c("cinza", f"  teto {human(timedelta(seconds=limit))}"))
            sys.stdout.flush()
        missing = limit - spent
        if missing <= 0:
            SCREEN.clear_line()
            return False
        try:
            proc.wait(timeout=min(missing, 1))
            SCREEN.clear_line()
            return True
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            continue


LIVE_LINE_INTERVAL = float(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_LINHA_VIVA", "30"))


# ── reading the queue ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def query_queue(name, repo):
    """`cepa-plan queue --max 1 --json`. Returns (data, error)."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(
            [sys.executable, str(CEPA_PLAN), "queue", name,
             "--max", "1", "--repo", str(repo), "--json"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return None, "o `cepa-plan queue` não respondeu em 60s"
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return None, (p.stderr or p.stdout or "").strip() or \
            f"`cepa-plan queue` saiu {p.returncode}"
    try:
        return json.loads(p.stdout), None
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        return None, f"o `cepa-plan queue` não devolveu JSON ({e})"


# How much of a blocked item's `evidence` the end-of-run summary shows. The command the
# owner needs to run tends to be at the end of the text ("I left X for you to
# run"), so the cut keeps the beginning AND the end, not just the beginning.
REASON_IN_SUMMARY = 600


def summarize_reason(text):
    text = " ".join(str(text).split())
    if len(text) <= REASON_IN_SUMMARY:
        return text
    half = REASON_IN_SUMMARY // 2
    return f"{text[:half]} [...] {text[-half:]}"


def read_item(plan_path, ident):
    """The item's current status on disk. The truth about the outcome is the PLAN, not the
    subprocess exit code — synchronize on the verifiable effect."""
    try:
        plan = yaml.safe_load(Path(plan_path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except Exception as e:
        return None, f"não consegui reler {plan_path}: {e}"
    for it in (plan or {}).get("items") or []:
        if isinstance(it, dict) and str(it.get("id")) == str(ident):
            return it, None
    return None, f"o item {ident} sumiu do plano durante o run"


# ── running an item ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def build_command(name, branch, permissions):
    # stream-json is what carries the `rate_limit_event` with the quota usage. `--verbose`
    # is required by `claude` itself for that format with `-p`.
    # `--na-branch` tells drain-plan that the tree it wakes up in IS the
    # night branch: no new worktree, commit straight onto it.
    request = f"/common:drain-plan {name} --max 1"
    if branch:
        request += f" --na-branch {branch}"
    cmd = ["claude", "-p", request,
           "--output-format", "stream-json", "--verbose"]
    if not permissions:
        cmd.append("--dangerously-skip-permissions")
    return cmd


def log_excerpt(log, since):
    """Everything ONE attempt wrote to the log. `since` is the size of the
    file before it started."""
    try:
        with open(log, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(since)
            raw = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return ""
    return raw.decode("utf-8", "replace")


def _json_objects(text, kind):
    """The stream-json lines of a `type`, in order. A line that is not JSON
    (text output, hook garbage) is ignored."""
    for line in text.splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if not line.startswith("{") or kind not in line:
            continue
        try:
            e = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("type") == kind:
            yield e


def _number(v):
    return isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool)


def quota_readings(text):
    """[(utilization, reset_epoch)] of the 5h window, one per `rate_limit_event`
    that carried the datum, in order."""
    readings = []
    for e in _json_objects(text, "rate_limit_event"):
        info = e.get("rate_limit_info") or {}
        w = (info.get("unifiedWindows") or {}).get("five_hour") \
            if isinstance(info, dict) else None
        if isinstance(w, dict) and _number(w.get("utilization")) \
                and _number(w.get("resetsAt")):
            readings.append((float(w["utilization"]), float(w["resetsAt"])))
    return readings


def round_costs(costs, text):
    """Adds to the `costs` dict ({key: US$}) each `result` block of `text`:
    one cost per `session_id`, and the LAST block of the session wins (the
    `total_cost_usd` is cumulative within the session; resuming the same session in a
    following round also comes out right). Order is that of first appearance.
    A block without `session_id` can't be deduplicated: each one counts.
    Reason (2026-10-13, leitura-de-guias-fase-0-c1): a single `claude -p`
    emitted 11 `result` blocks of the same session and summing them all gave US$ 334.94
    instead of 50.25."""
    for r in _json_objects(text, "result"):
        v = r.get("total_cost_usd")
        if not _number(v):
            continue
        sid = r.get("session_id")
        key = sid if isinstance(sid, str) and sid else ("", len(costs))
        costs[key] = float(v)
    return costs


def reset_time(text, now):
    """The announced reset in text ("resets 3:20am (America/Sao_Paulo)") as a
    naive local datetime, at the next occurrence. None if it can't be known."""
    m = RESET_HOUR.search(text or "")
    if not m:
        return None
    hh, mm, ap, tz_name = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2) or 0), m.group(3), m.group(4)
    if not 1 <= hh <= 12 or mm > 59:
        return None
    hh = hh % 12 + (12 if ap.lower() == "p" else 0)
    tz = None
    if tz_name:
        try:
            from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo
            tz = ZoneInfo(tz_name.strip())
        except Exception:
            tz = None
    base = datetime.now(tz) if tz else now
    target = base.replace(hour=hh, minute=mm, second=0, microsecond=0)
    # Announced a few minutes ago is the reset of now, not tomorrow's.
    if target < base - timedelta(minutes=10):
        target += timedelta(days=1)
    if tz:
        target = target.astimezone().replace(tzinfo=None)
    return target


def usage_limit(output):
    """(hit, reset_text, reset_at) over the output of ONE attempt.

    The structured signal comes first: a `rate_limit_event` with status
    `rejected` is the exhausted account, and no agent prose imitates it. Without
    it, the text: the final `result` of the stream-json or, in text output, its
    end (see OUTPUT_TAIL). `reset_text` is the verbatim time for the
    report; `reset_at` is the same time as a datetime, or None."""
    rejected = [e.get("rate_limit_info") or {}
                  for e in _json_objects(output or "", "rate_limit_event")
                  if (e.get("rate_limit_info") or {}).get("status") == "rejected"]
    if rejected:
        r = rejected[-1].get("resetsAt")
        reset_dt = datetime.fromtimestamp(r) if _number(r) else None
        return True, (reset_dt.strftime("%H:%M") if reset_dt else None), reset_dt
    results = [e.get("result") for e in _json_objects(output or "", "result")
                  if isinstance(e.get("result"), str)]
    text = results[-1] if results else (output or "")[-OUTPUT_TAIL:]
    if not text or not USAGE_LIMIT.search(text):
        return False, None, None
    m = LIMIT_RESET.search(text)
    reset = m.group(1).strip().rstrip(".") if m else None
    return True, reset, reset_time(text, datetime.now())


def item_cost(starts):
    """The largest jump in usage between the start readings of two consecutive
    items in the SAME 5h window. None without a measured pair."""
    jumps = [b[0] - a[0] for a, b in zip(starts, starts[1:])
              if a[1] == b[1] and b[0] >= a[0]]
    return max(jumps) if jumps else None


def quota_pause(reading, fresh, cost, now):
    """The reset to wait for before starting the next item, or None to proceed.

    `reading` is the last (usage, reset_epoch) seen. `fresh` says whether it came
    AFTER the previous item started; if not, the previous item isn't in it yet,
    and the projection adds its cost too."""
    if not reading:
        return None
    usage, reset_epoch = reading
    reset = datetime.fromtimestamp(reset_epoch)
    if reset <= now:
        return None
    if cost is None:
        return reset if usage >= QUOTA_WITHOUT_HISTORY else None
    projected = usage + cost * (1 if fresh else 2)
    return reset if projected > 1.0 else None


def wait_until(when):
    """Sleeps until `when` by the wall clock, in short steps: `time.sleep`
    doesn't advance while the machine is suspended, the clock does."""
    while True:
        missing = (when - datetime.now()).total_seconds()
        if missing <= 0:
            return
        time.sleep(min(missing, 60))


def network_drop(output):
    """True if the attempt died because `claude` couldn't reach the API — the final
    `result` carries `terminal_reason: api_error` AND the message is a network one.
    An item that closed doesn't go through here; the loop decides that."""
    results = list(_json_objects(output or "", "result"))
    if not results:
        return False
    r = results[-1]
    if r.get("terminal_reason") != "api_error" and not r.get("is_error"):
        return False
    text = r.get("result") if isinstance(r.get("result"), str) else ""
    return bool(NO_NETWORK.search(text))


def network_reachable(target=None, timeout=5):
    """Opens a TCP connection to `host:port` and closes it. False on any error:
    DNS, refusal, timeout."""
    host, _, port = (target or NETWORK_PROBE).rpartition(":")
    try:
        with socket.create_connection((host, int(port)), timeout=timeout):
            return True
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False


def wait_for_network(until_at, probe=network_reachable, interval=None):
    """Probes until the network is back or until `until_at` (wall clock). Returns True
    if it came back."""
    step = PROBE_INTERVAL if interval is None else interval
    while True:
        if probe():
            return True
        missing = (until_at - datetime.now()).total_seconds()
        if missing <= 0:
            return False
        time.sleep(max(min(missing, step), 0.05))


def item_environment():
    """The environment of ONE window subprocess: the mark that turns on the window's
    hooks, and the background-wait ceiling zeroed (see ENV_BG_WAIT)."""
    env = dict(os.environ, **{ENV_WINDOW: "1"})
    env.setdefault(ENV_BG_WAIT, "0")
    return env


def installed_twg_version():
    """Version of the `twg` CLI (Atlassian) installed right now, or None if absent from
    PATH / `--version` fails / the output has nothing that looks like a version.

    Read at every item (never cached in `run_start`): `twg` runs a
    scheduler (`com.atlassian.twg.upkeep`) that checks for updates on its own
    every 12 minutes, and the version can change BETWEEN two items of the same run with
    no signal at all — which is exactly the vector this record exists to catch.
    A short timeout and any exception become None: a third-party CLI can't
    take the run down.
    """
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["twg", "--version"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
        return None
    m = re.search(r"\d+(?:\.\d+)+", (p.stdout or "") + (p.stderr or ""))
    return m.group(0) if m else None


def run_item(name, tree, branch, permissions, limit_sec, log,
                 on_launch=None):
    """Launches ONE subprocess, with `tree` (the night worktree) as cwd.
    Returns (code, killed_by_timeout, seconds, this_attempt_output).
    `on_launch` receives the child's pid: it is what `run_interrompido` says
    was left running."""
    repo = tree
    cmd = build_command(name, branch, permissions)
    start = time.monotonic()
    try:
        mark = os.path.getsize(log)
    except OSError:
        mark = 0
    with open(log, "ab", buffering=0) as output:
        output.write(f"\n===== {datetime.now().isoformat(timespec='seconds')} "
                    f"· {' '.join(cmd)}\n".encode("utf-8"))
        output.flush()
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=str(repo), stdout=output,
                                    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                                    stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                    env=item_environment(),
                                    start_new_session=True)
        except OSError as e:
            # `claude` vanished from PATH, lost its permission or the binary is
            # corrupted AFTER launch. Blowing up here would kill the supervisor
            # and the window along with it, leaving the record half-written — the opposite of
            # what it exists to do. It becomes an item with no progress: the circuit breaker
            # ends it at 3, with the reason written.
            output.write(f"MAESTRO-SPAWN-FALHOU: {e}\n".encode("utf-8"))
            return -2, False, time.monotonic() - start, ""
        if on_launch:
            on_launch(proc.pid)
        if wait_for_child(proc, limit_sec, "claude"):
            code = proc.returncode
            killed = False
        else:
            # Kills the GROUP: claude spawns children (builds, mvn), and killing only the
            # parent leaves an orphan build holding the tree.
            killed = True
            try:
                os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGTERM)
                proc.wait(timeout=SIGTERM_GRACE)
            except Exception:
                try:
                    os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
                except Exception:
                    pass
            code = proc.returncode if proc.returncode is not None else -1
    return code, killed, time.monotonic() - start, log_excerpt(log, mark)


def terminate_group(pid, grace):
    """Ends the child's group (`claude` and what it launched: builds, mvn),
    which runs in its own session and doesn't receive the terminal's signal. SIGTERM, up to
    `grace` seconds, and SIGKILL on whatever is left. Returns whether the group ended."""
    try:
        os.killpg(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return True
    except PermissionError:
        pass  # all-zombie group (EPERM note below): the loop reaps and confirms
    except OSError:
        return False
    end = time.monotonic() + grace
    while True:
        try:
            os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)
        except ChildProcessError:
            pass
        # macOS: killpg(pgid, 0) gives EPERM while the group only holds processes that
        # exited and were not reaped yet (ESRCH once it dissolves). The loop keeps polling
        # while the group is all-zombie; the SIGKILL block below is what declares it dead.
        try:
            os.killpg(pid, 0)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            return True
        except PermissionError:
            if time.monotonic() >= end:
                break
            time.sleep(0.05)
            continue
        except OSError:
            return False
        if time.monotonic() >= end:
            break
        time.sleep(0.1)
    try:
        os.killpg(pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        os.waitpid(pid, 0)
    except (ChildProcessError, ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
        pass  # PermissionError: all-zombie group (see the EPERM note above) = dead
    except OSError:
        return False
    return True


def block_item(name, repo, ident, attempts, side_branch=None):
    """Takes out of the queue's way the item that spent its attempt ceiling.
    Returns None if it succeeded, or the error as text.

    This is the ONLY point where the supervisor WRITES to the plan, and the exception is
    deliberate. What it records here — "this item has already consumed N subprocesses
    of THIS window" — is a fact that only exists at this level: each subprocess is born
    with no memory of the previous one, which is precisely what makes 12h possible, so
    neither `/common:drain-plan` nor `cepa-plan` has any way to see the repetition.
    Without the mark, `queue` re-offers the same item forever.

    `blocked` is the right state and is not a new state: `build_batch` DEFERS
    `blocked` and moves on to the next item, which is exactly the semantics wanted,
    and `finish` already clears `claimed_by` — the orphan reservation doesn't hang around.
    """
    evidence = (
        f"{attempts} tentativas seguidas do `cepa-until` na mesma janela sem "
        "tirar o item do lugar. Isto NÃO é veredito sobre o trabalho nem "
        "condição de fora: é o supervisor tirando o item da frente para a fila "
        "andar. A saída do `claude` de cada tentativa está no `.log` do run; "
        "devolva o item para `pending` quando souber o que travou.")
    if side_branch:
        evidence += (f" Os commits das tentativas, que não passaram pelo "
                      f"build do supervisor, estão em `{side_branch}`.")
    impede = (f"o executor tentou {attempts} vezes seguidas e o item não "
              "andou. Ninguém investigou o motivo ainda.")
    return finish_item(name, repo, ident, "blocked", evidence, impede)


# ── start-up guards ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# What counts as dirt is defined once in hooks/_dirt.py (shared with cepa-doctor and
# the safe-exit-gate hook); the names stay here because tests and the guard use them.
RUN_RECORD = _dirt.RUN_RECORD
QUEUE_BAK = _dirt.QUEUE_BAK


# The `plan.yaml` modified on disk. Only the ` M` (uncommitted, unstaged):
# it is how `cepa-plan start/finish` leaves it.
PLAN_MODIFIED = re.compile(
    r"^ M (\.claude/(?:programs/([^/]+)/plan|queues/([^/]+)/queue)\.yaml)$")
# The fields that `cepa-plan start/finish` of a live run writes on the item.
RUN_FIELDS = ("status", "claimed_by", "evidence")


def plan_only_from_live_run(repo, path, queue):
    """Is the modified `plan.yaml` of `queue` only what its LIVE run wrote?
    On 2026-10-15 19:08 the owner launched `cepa-until --until 6:00 cepa` with a run
    of the same queue running (pid 16795), and the dirty-tree refusal blamed the
    `status`/`claimed_by` that the run itself was writing (fb-20261015-4). It only holds if
    the difference against HEAD is limited to `status`, `claimed_by` and `evidence`
    of items the run started (`item_start` in its record); any other
    difference, or unreadable YAML, remains dirt."""
    alive = live_run_of_queue(repo, queue)
    if not alive:
        return False
    code, before = git(["show", f"HEAD:{path}"], repo)
    if code != 0:
        return False
    try:
        before = yaml.safe_load(before)
        after = yaml.safe_load(
            (Path(repo) / path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, yaml.YAMLError):
        return False
    if not (isinstance(before, dict) and isinstance(after, dict)):
        return False
    items_a, items_d = before.get("items"), after.get("items")
    if not (isinstance(items_a, list) and isinstance(items_d, list)):
        return False
    if {k: v for k, v in before.items() if k != "items"} != \
            {k: v for k, v in after.items() if k != "items"}:
        return False
    if len(items_a) != len(items_d):
        return False
    for a, d in zip(items_a, items_d):
        if not (isinstance(a, dict) and isinstance(d, dict)):
            return False
        if a.get("id") != d.get("id"):
            return False
        if str(a.get("id")) in alive["iniciados"]:
            a = {k: v for k, v in a.items() if k not in RUN_FIELDS}
            d = {k: v for k, v in d.items() if k not in RUN_FIELDS}
        if a != d:
            return False
    return True


def dirty_tree(repo, live_run_ok=False):
    """The `git status` lines that count as dirt. With `live_run_ok`,
    the `plan.yaml` that a live run of the queue itself is writing doesn't count
    (see `plan_only_from_live_run`); other callers stay strict."""
    try:
        # `--untracked-files=all`, like `_dirt.dirt` and the doctor: a collapsed
        # `?? .claude/` hid the run record this filter exists to ignore, so the
        # safe-exit gate let "Safe to exit" through and this guard refused
        # (completion-auditor gap AC5, item wrap-up-safe-to-exit-exige-clone-limpo).
        p = subprocess.run(["git", "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all"],
                           cwd=str(repo), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except Exception:
        return None
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return None

    def only_the_run(line):
        m = PLAN_MODIFIED.match(line)
        return bool(live_run_ok and m
                    and plan_only_from_live_run(repo, m.group(1),
                                             m.group(2) or m.group(3)))

    return [l for l in p.stdout.splitlines()
            if _dirt.counts_as_dirt(l) and not only_the_run(l)]


def touched_by_last_run(repo, queue):
    """The files the last run of this queue committed on the night branch
    (`base..branch` of the most recent `run_start`). With no record, or with the branch
    already deleted, returns empty: nothing on disk can have come from the run."""
    d = qp.queue_dir(repo, queue) / "until"
    for reg in sorted(d.glob("*.jsonl"), reverse=True):
        start_point = None
        try:
            for l in reg.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
                ev = json.loads(l) if l.strip() else {}
                if ev.get("evento") == "run_start":
                    start_point = ev
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if not (start_point and start_point.get("base") and start_point.get("branch")):
            continue
        # `-z` on both sides: without it git writes `relatório.md` as
        # `"relat\303\263rio.md"`, and the name never matches the one on disk.
        p = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "--name-only", "-z",
                            f"{start_point['base']}..{start_point['branch']}"],
                           cwd=str(repo), capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=30)
        return set(filter(None, p.stdout.split("\0"))) \
            if p.returncode == 0 else set()
    return set()


def vanished_from_disk(repo):
    """A committed file that is no longer on disk, without the staged deletion
    (git status's ` D`), with the raw name."""
    p = subprocess.run(["git", "ls-files", "--deleted", "-z"], cwd=str(repo),
                       capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    return list(filter(None, p.stdout.split("\0"))) if p.returncode == 0 else []


def ghost_deletions(repo, queue):
    """A committed file that vanished from disk and that the last run didn't touch. On
    09/14 Insync deleted 9 committed files from the main clone with no
    Claude process running; the refusal blamed the run and suggested `--dirty-ok`,
    which would have let the next item run on top of the missing folder."""
    vanished = vanished_from_disk(repo)
    if not vanished:
        return []
    touched = touched_by_last_run(repo, queue)
    return [f for f in vanished if f not in touched]


def restore_targets(repo, files):
    """The highest folder that vanished whole, instead of file by file."""
    targets = []
    for f in files:
        target = Path(f)
        while target.parent != Path(".") and not (repo / target.parent).exists():
            target = target.parent
        if str(target) not in targets:
            targets.append(str(target))
    return targets


def read_branch(repo):
    """(branch, error). Error is what git said: on 09/25 the usual `"?"`
    hid a `fatal: not a git repository` and the loop read a branch switch."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD"],
                           cwd=str(repo), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except Exception as e:
        return None, str(e)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return None, (p.stderr.strip() or f"`git rev-parse` saiu {p.returncode}")
    return p.stdout.strip(), None


def current_branch(repo):
    branch, _ = read_branch(repo)
    return branch or "?"


# ── the night branch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def git(args, cwd, timeout=120):
    """(code, stdout+stderr). Never raises: the supervisor doesn't die over git."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["git", *args], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=timeout)
        return p.returncode, (p.stdout + p.stderr).strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return 1, str(e)


def head_of(tree):
    code, output = git(["rev-parse", "HEAD"], tree)
    return output if code == 0 else None


def inheritance_from_previous_run(repo, queue, plan_path):
    """The branches of previous runs that hold commits of an item that
    was left half-done and that the clone doesn't have yet. List of
    {"branch", "itens", "commits"}, from oldest to newest.

    On 09/27 WEGO-2283 was killed by the slack with 15 commits on
    `until/2026-09-27-1632`. The next run was born from the clone's HEAD, `start`
    claimed the orphan reservation and the item restarted from zero, because its commits
    were on the previous night's branch. The run record is what knows
    where they are: for each item still open in the queue, the newest `.jsonl`
    that ran it names the branch, and `item_end` says whether there was a commit."""
    try:
        plan = yaml.safe_load(Path(plan_path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, TypeError, yaml.YAMLError):
        return []
    open_items = {str(it.get("id")) for it in (plan or {}).get("items") or []
               if str(it.get("status") or "pending").strip().lower()
               not in TERMINAL_STATES}
    d = qp.queue_dir(repo, queue) / "until"
    seen, by_branch = set(), {}
    for reg in sorted(d.glob("*.jsonl"), reverse=True):
        try:
            events = [json.loads(l) for l in
                       reg.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if l.strip()]
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        branch = next((e.get("branch") for e in events
                       if e.get("evento") == "run_start"), None)
        ends = {}
        for e in events:
            if e.get("evento") == "item_end" and str(e.get("id")) in open_items:
                ends.setdefault(str(e["id"]), []).append(e)
        for ident, items_list in ends.items():
            if ident in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(ident)
            if branch and any((e.get("commits") or 0) > 0 for e in items_list):
                by_branch.setdefault((reg.name, branch), []).append(ident)
    inheritance = []
    for (_, branch), items in sorted(by_branch.items()):
        if git(["rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"refs/heads/{branch}"],
               repo)[0] != 0:
            continue
        if git(["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", branch, "HEAD"], repo)[0] == 0:
            continue
        c, n = git(["rev-list", "--count", f"HEAD..{branch}"], repo)
        inheritance.append({"branch": branch, "itens": sorted(items),
                        "commits": int(n) if c == 0 and n.isdigit() else None})
    return inheritance


def open_run_branch(repo, run_id, inheritance=()):
    """Creates `until/<run>` from the clone's HEAD and its worktree outside the
    synced tree, and merges into it the `inheritance` branches. Returns
    (tree, branch, error). On error, neither worktree nor branch is left behind."""
    branch = f"until/{run_id}"
    home = Path(os.environ.get(ENV_WORKTREE_HOME)
                or Path.home() / "cepa-worktrees")
    tree = home / f"{repo.name}-until-{run_id}"
    home.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    code, output = git(["worktree", "add", "-q", "-b", branch, str(tree),
                         "HEAD"], repo)
    if code != 0:
        return None, branch, output or f"`git worktree add` saiu {code}"
    for h in inheritance:
        code, output = git(["merge", "--no-edit", h["branch"]], tree)
        if code != 0:
            git(["merge", "--abort"], tree)
            git(["worktree", "remove", "--force", str(tree)], repo)
            git(["branch", "-D", branch], repo)
            return None, branch, (
                f"a branch `{h['branch']}` guarda commits de "
                f"{', '.join(h['itens'])}, que ficou pela metade no run "
                f"anterior, e não mescla com o HEAD do clone:\n{output[-800:]}\n"
                f"Mescle à mão no clone (`git merge {h['branch']}`), resolva o "
                "conflito e rode de novo. Começar sem ela faria o item "
                "recomeçar do zero")
    return tree, branch, None


def repair_link(repo, tree, branch):
    """Rebuilds `.git/worktrees/<name>`, the folder that links the night worktree to the
    clone, when it vanished and the worktree stayed on disk (WEGO run of 09/25: the
    whole folder vanished at 00:2x, Insync suspected). `git worktree repair`
    doesn't help: without the folder it refuses ("unable to locate repository").

    It only recreates what `git worktree add` would have created — HEAD pointing to the
    launch branch, `commondir`, `gitdir` — and rebuilds the index from
    HEAD without touching the files. Returns None if repaired, or the reason."""
    pointer = Path(tree) / ".git"
    if not pointer.is_file():
        return f"`{pointer}` não existe: a worktree da noite sumiu do disco"
    line = pointer.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").strip()
    if not line.startswith("gitdir:"):
        return f"`{pointer}` não aponta para um gitdir: {line[:120]!r}"
    admin = Path(line[len("gitdir:"):].strip())
    if not admin.is_absolute():
        admin = (Path(tree) / admin).resolve()
    code, common_dir = git(["rev-parse", "--git-common-dir"], repo)
    if code != 0:
        return f"o clone também não responde ao git: {common_dir}"
    common_dir = Path(common_dir) if Path(common_dir).is_absolute() else Path(repo) / common_dir
    home = common_dir.resolve() / "worktrees"
    if admin.parent.resolve() != home:
        return (f"`{pointer}` aponta para `{admin}`, fora de `{home}`: "
                "não recrio ligação em lugar que não é do clone")
    if admin.exists():
        return f"`{admin}` existe e mesmo assim o git não responde"
    code, output = git(["rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"refs/heads/{branch}"],
                        repo)
    if code != 0:
        return f"a branch `{branch}` não existe mais no clone"
    try:
        admin.mkdir(parents=True)
        (admin / "HEAD").write_text(f"ref: refs/heads/{branch}\n")
        (admin / "commondir").write_text(f"{os.path.relpath(common_dir.resolve(), admin)}\n")
        (admin / "gitdir").write_text(f"{pointer.resolve()}\n")
    except OSError as e:
        return f"não consegui recriar `{admin}`: {e}"
    code, output = git(["reset", "-q"], tree)
    if code != 0:
        return f"recriei `{admin}`, mas `git reset` saiu {code}: {output}"
    return None


def changed_hooks(tree, since):
    """Plugin hooks that the night branch changed since `since`.

    Hooks run from the plugin installed in the cache, which is a copy of the clone at the
    last install, and not from the night branch. In run 2026-09-28-1146 items
    1 and 2 fixed `no-background-build` and `bash-path-lock`, and the next
    4 rounds were still blocked by the old versions with nothing
    in the run saying so. A hook is a file under `<plugin>/hooks/`, where `<plugin>`
    has `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`; in a repo that is not a plugin the list
    always comes out empty."""
    if not since:
        return []
    c, output = git(["diff", "--name-only", f"{since}..HEAD"], tree)
    if c != 0:
        return []
    found = []
    for line in output.splitlines():
        parts = line.strip().split("/")
        if (len(parts) >= 3 and parts[1] == "hooks"
                and (tree / parts[0] / ".claude-plugin" / "plugin.json")
                .is_file()):
            found.append(line.strip())
    return found


def close_empty_branch(repo, tree, branch, base):
    """A night with no commit at all leaves no worktree or branch behind."""
    if head_of(tree) != base or dirty_tree(tree):
        return False
    git(["worktree", "remove", str(tree)], repo)
    git(["branch", "-D", branch], repo)
    return True


def stash_leftover(tree, run_id, ident):
    """The item finished with uncommitted files. The next card can't
    start on top of them, and the full build would measure the leftovers instead of what was
    committed. Stores them in a stash with a unique label and returns its sha."""
    tag = f"cepa-until {run_id} {ident}"
    code, output = git(["stash", "push", "-u", "-m", tag], tree)
    if code != 0:
        return None, output
    code, items_list = git(["stash", "list", "--format=%H %gs"], tree)
    for line in items_list.splitlines():
        if line.endswith(tag):
            return line.split()[0], None
    return None, "stash criado mas não encontrado pela etiqueta"


def verify_command(repo, explicit, waived):
    """(command, origin). Command None = waived; '' = don't know which it is."""
    if waived:
        return None, "--no-verify"
    if explicit:
        return explicit, "--verify"
    if (repo / ".claude" / "no-build").exists():
        if (repo / SUITE_WITHOUT_BUILD).exists():
            return SUITE_WITHOUT_BUILD, (f"achei `{SUITE_WITHOUT_BUILD}`; o "
                                     "`.claude/no-build` só dispensa o build")
        return None, ".claude/no-build"
    for file_path, command in VERIFY_BY_FILE:
        if (repo / file_path).exists():
            return command, f"achei `{file_path}` na raiz"
    js = javascript_verify(repo)
    if js:
        return js
    return "", None


def run_verify(command, tree, limit_sec, log, on_launch=None):
    """Runs the full build on the night branch, with the output going to the run's `.log`.
    Returns (green, seconds, reason)."""
    start = time.monotonic()
    with open(log, "ab", buffering=0) as output:
        output.write(f"\n===== {datetime.now().isoformat(timespec='seconds')} "
                    f"· verify · {command}\n".encode("utf-8"))
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen(command, shell=True, cwd=str(tree),
                                    stdout=output, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                                    stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                    start_new_session=True)
        except OSError as e:
            return False, time.monotonic() - start, f"não lançou: {e}"
        if on_launch:
            on_launch(proc.pid)
        if wait_for_child(proc, limit_sec, "build"):
            code = proc.returncode
        else:
            try:
                os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
            except Exception:
                pass
            proc.wait()
            return False, time.monotonic() - start, "não terminou dentro da janela"
    spent = time.monotonic() - start
    return code == 0, spent, (None if code == 0 else f"saiu {code}")


def undo_item(repo, tree, run_id, ident, since, in_the_middle=(),
                suffix="vermelho", back=1):
    """Takes off the night branch the commits of an item whose build went
    red, without losing them: they stay in `until/<run>-<suffix>-<id>`.

    `since` is the HEAD at the start of the item's FIRST attempt in this window, and
    not that of the last: WEGO-2320 took two attempts, and the reset to the start
    of the second left the first one's 9 commits on the night branch without ever
    going through the build (A5/C4). Resetting that far is only safe with two
    checks, and if one fails the supervisor returns the error instead of resetting:
    `since` must be an ancestor of HEAD, and no other item may have closed
    `done` since then (`in_the_middle`), because the reset would erase that item's
    green work."""
    if not since:
        return None, f"não li o HEAD do começo da 1ª tentativa do {ident}"
    if in_the_middle:
        return None, (
            f"voltar a branch da noite para {since[:10]}, o começo da 1ª "
            f"tentativa do {ident}, apagaria o trabalho de "
            f"{', '.join(in_the_middle)}, que entrou depois dele")
    code, _ = git(["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", since, "HEAD"], tree)
    if code != 0:
        return None, (f"{since[:10]}, o começo da 1ª tentativa do {ident}, "
                      "não é ancestral do HEAD da branch da noite")
    # The 2nd return of the same item in the same run can't overwrite the side branch of the
    # 1st: it holds commits the agent may not have used.
    side_branch = (f"until/{run_id}-{suffix}-{ident}"
               + (f"-v{back}" if back > 1 else ""))
    code, output = git(["branch", "-f", side_branch, "HEAD"], tree)
    if code != 0:
        return None, output
    code, output = git(["reset", "-q", "--hard", since], tree)
    if code != 0:
        return None, output
    return side_branch, None


def red_returns(ledger_dir, ident):
    """How many red returns the item has already had, counted in the `.jsonl` of ALL
    the queue's runs: the ceiling holds across runs, and without a new file."""
    n = 0
    for reg in ledger_dir.glob("*.jsonl"):
        try:
            lines = reg.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines()
        except OSError:
            continue
        for line in lines:
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if (isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("evento") == "volta_vermelha"
                    and str(e.get("id")) == str(ident)):
                n += 1
    return n


# The side branches the supervisor creates: `until/<run>-vermelho-<id>[-v<n>]` on a
# red build, `until/<run>-parado-<id>` on the item that spent its attempts and
# `until/<run>-travado-<id>` on the item the agent closed `blocked` with commits.
SIDE_BRANCH = re.compile(
    r"^until/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{4}-(?:vermelho|parado|travado)-(.+?)"
    r"(?:-v\d+)?$")


def clean_side_branches(repo, plan_path, destination, run_branch):
    """Deletes the side branches of `done` or `dropped` items, but only after
    writing to `destination` the `git format-patch` of the commits that the night branch
    doesn't have (Revision 3, 4f). Without the patch on disk, the branch stays: the owner asked
    not to have anything to remember, and not to lose code.

    Returns [(branch, patch, error)]; `patch` None when the branch stayed."""
    code, output = git(["for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname:short)",
                         "refs/heads/until/"], repo)
    if code != 0:
        return []
    try:
        items = (yaml.safe_load(Path(plan_path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
                 or {}).get("items") or []
    except (OSError, TypeError, yaml.YAMLError):
        return []
    status = {str(it.get("id")): str(it.get("status") or "").lower()
              for it in items if isinstance(it, dict)}
    done_items = []
    for branch in output.splitlines():
        m = SIDE_BRANCH.match(branch.strip())
        if not m or status.get(m.group(1)) not in ("done", "dropped"):
            continue
        file_path = destination / (branch[len("until/"):] + ".patch")
        try:
            destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            with open(file_path, "wb") as f:
                p = subprocess.run(["git", "format-patch", "--stdout",
                                    f"{run_branch}..{branch}"], cwd=str(repo),
                                   stdout=f, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,
                                   timeout=120)
            error = (None if p.returncode == 0 else
                    (p.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
                     or f"format-patch saiu {p.returncode}"))
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            error = str(e)
        if error:
            try:
                file_path.unlink()
            except OSError:
                pass
            done_items.append((branch, None, error))
            continue
        code, output_d = git(["branch", "-D", branch], repo)
        done_items.append((branch, str(file_path) if code == 0 else None,
                       None if code == 0 else output_d))
    return done_items


def emit_telemetry(event, repo, **fields):
    """An event in the ledger of `~/.claude/cepa-telemetry/`, through the same module
    as the hooks. Never takes the run down: telemetry is a network, not a gate."""
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / "hooks"))
        import _telemetry
        _telemetry.emit(event, cwd=str(repo), **fields)
    except Exception:
        pass


def finish_item(name, repo, ident, status, evidence, impede=None, owner=None):
    """`cepa-plan finish`. Returns None or the error as text. `impede` is the
    human section's reason, required by `cepa-plan` on `blocked`; `owner` is a
    whole human section to carry over (`finish` replaces it)."""
    owner = dict(owner or {})
    if impede:
        owner["impede"] = impede
    flags = []
    for key, flag, _ in _ownertext.FIELDS:
        if str(owner.get(key) or "").strip():
            flags += [flag, str(owner[key])]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(
            [sys.executable, str(CEPA_PLAN), "finish", name, str(ident),
             "--status", status, "--evidence", evidence, "--repo", str(repo)]
            + flags,
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:
        return f"o `cepa-plan finish` não respondeu: {e}"
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return (p.stderr or p.stdout or "").strip() or \
            f"`cepa-plan finish` saiu {p.returncode}"
    return None


# ── the end-of-run analysis ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

def analyze_run(repo, tree, ledger, permissions):
    """Runs `/common:until-review` over the run and writes `<run>.review.md`.
    Returns (path, error)."""
    destination = ledger.with_suffix(".review.md")
    cmd = ["claude", "-p", f"/common:until-review {ledger}",
           "--output-format", "text"]
    if not permissions:
        cmd.append("--dangerously-skip-permissions")
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=str(tree or repo), capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=ANALYSIS_LIMIT_SEC,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=item_environment())
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return None, f"não terminou em {ANALYSIS_LIMIT_SEC // 60} min"
    except OSError as e:
        return None, f"não lançou: {e}"
    if p.returncode != 0 or not p.stdout.strip():
        return None, (p.stderr or "").strip()[-300:] or f"saiu {p.returncode}"
    destination.write_text(p.stdout, encoding="utf-8")
    return destination, None


# ── the loop ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── aterrissar: the owner takes the night branch to the clone's branch ──────

WORKTREE_GUARD = HERE.parent / "hooks" / "worktree-guard.py"
WTLIB = HERE.parent / "hooks" / "_wtlib.py"


SUBCOMMANDS = [
    ("pendentes", "lists the runs waiting for the owner and the runs whose "
                  "supervisor died"),
    ("decide", "asks, one at a time, what a run or the queue left for the owner"),
    ("aterrissar", "lands the run branch on the clone's branch: merge, full "
                   "build and push"),
    ("fecha-morto", "runs the missing full build of a run whose supervisor "
                    "died and leaves it ready to land"),
]


def _sub_summary(name):
    return dict(SUBCOMMANDS)[name]


def land_parser():
    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa until aterrissar",
        summary=_sub_summary("aterrissar"),
        description=(
            "Brings the run branch (until/<run>) into the branch the clone is on.\n"
            "Before touching anything it checks that the run proposed the landing,\n"
            "that no other live session holds either branch, that both trees are\n"
            "clean and that the run branch did not move after the proposal.\n"
            "\n"
            "It stops on a merge conflict, never pushes a red build (a red build\n"
            "rolls the clone's branch back to where it was), and running it again\n"
            "resumes where it stopped: with the merge done, it goes on from the\n"
            "build. On success it removes the run worktree and branch.\n"
            "Without --yes, it only shows the plan."),
        examples=[
            ("cepa until aterrissar wego/2026-11-03-2210", "show the landing plan"),
            ("cepa until aterrissar wego/2026-11-03-2210 --yes", "merge, build and push"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "landed, already landed, or plan shown (without --yes)"),
            (2, "invalid usage, target not <queue>/<run>, or run state unreadable"),
            (3, "refused: run not waiting for landing, wrong branch, dirty tree, "
                "another live session, branch moved or gone, merge failed"),
            (4, "merge conflict: resolve, commit and run again"),
            (5, "red build after the merge: clone branch rolled back, nothing pushed"),
            (6, "push failed: the merge and the green build stay; run again"),
        ],
        see_also=["cepa until pendentes: which runs are waiting to land",
                  "cepa until decide: the questions the run left, landing included"])
    ap.add_argument("target", metavar="QUEUE/RUN",
                    help="the run to land, as the run summary prints it")
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=".", metavar="DIR",
                    help="repository root (default: the current directory)")
    ap.add_argument("--yes", "--sim", dest="yes", action="store_true",
                    help="executes; without it, only shows the plan")
    return ap


def cmd_land(argv):
    """`cepa-until aterrissar <queue>/<run> [--yes]` — step 3 of
    until-fim-sem-dono.

    The run doesn't touch the main branch (owner's decision 3, 09/26): whoever triggers
    the landing is the owner, and this command is a thin layer over the guards that
    already exist (C3 of `docs/estrategia-fim-do-cepa-until.md`): single owner via
    `worktree-guard.py`, stop on conflict, never push with a red
    build, record the return point and refuse if the night branch moved
    after the proposal. Running again resumes where it stopped: with the merge already
    done, it continues from the build. Without `--yes`, it only shows the plan."""
    ap = land_parser()
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if "/" not in a.target:
        print("cepa-until aterrissar: o alvo é <fila>/<run> (ex.: "
              "cepa/2026-09-28-2137)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    queue, run_id = a.target.split("/", 1)
    repo = Path(a.repo).resolve()
    path = qp.queue_dir(repo, queue) / "until" / \
        f"{run_id}.estado.json"
    try:
        item_states = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"cepa-until aterrissar: não li o estado do run em {path} "
              f"({e})", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    def record(**fields):
        item_states.update(fields)
        item_states["atualizado"] = datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
        tmp = path.parent / (path.name + ".tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(item_states, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n",
                       encoding="utf-8")
        os.replace(tmp, path)

    def refuse(text):
        print(f"cepa-until aterrissar: {text}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    if item_states.get("estado") == "aterrissado":
        print(f"o run {run_id} já foi aterrissado "
              f"({(item_states.get('aterrissagem') or {}).get('quando', '?')})")
        return 0
    if item_states.get("estado") != "esperando-dono":
        return refuse(f"o run {run_id} está `{item_states.get('estado')}`, e só se "
                      "aterrissa um run `esperando-dono`")
    action = next((x for x in item_states.get("acoes") or []
                 if x.get("id") == "aterrissar"), None)
    if not action:
        return refuse(f"o run {run_id} não propôs `aterrissar` (a branch da "
                      "noite ficou sem commit)")
    branch, destination = item_states.get("branch"), action.get("destino")
    sha, tree = action.get("sha"), action.get("arvore")
    landing_info = dict(item_states.get("aterrissagem") or {})

    # Already merged (the owner resolved a conflict and concluded the merge, or the
    # previous attempt stopped after it): continue from the build.
    code, _ = git(["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", sha, "HEAD"], repo)
    already_merged = code == 0

    current = current_branch(repo)
    if current != destination:
        return refuse(f"o clone está em `{current}`, e a ação foi proposta para "
                      f"`{destination}`. Volte para `{destination}` e rode de novo")
    if not already_merged:
        code, now = git(["rev-parse", branch], repo)
        if code != 0:
            return refuse(f"a branch da noite `{branch}` não existe mais")
        if now != sha:
            return refuse(
                f"a branch da noite `{branch}` mudou desde que a ação foi "
                f"proposta ({sha[:10]} → {now[:10]}). O que entrou depois "
                "do fim do run não passou pelo build do supervisor; confira "
                "e rode um novo run, ou volte a branch para o SHA proposto")

    print(f"aterrissar `{branch}` em `{destination}` ({repo})")
    print(f"  efeito : {action.get('frase')}")
    print(f"  build  : {item_states.get('verify') or 'nenhum (o run dispensou o build)'}")
    print("  push   : " + ("sim, para o upstream de "
                           f"`{destination}`" if has_upstream(repo) else
                           f"não (`{destination}` não tem upstream)"))
    if already_merged:
        print("  merge  : já feito; retomo do build")
    if not a.yes:
        print(f"\nnada foi feito. Para executar: cepa-until aterrissar "
              f"{a.target} --yes")
        return 0

    # Single owner (the same guard as /common:worktree-merge). Before the
    # dirty-tree check: the session registry lives in `.claude/sessions/`.
    try:
        g = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(WORKTREE_GUARD), branch,
                            "--cwd", str(repo),
                            "--exclude-cwd", os.getcwd()],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        guard_output = g.stdout.strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return refuse(f"não consegui rodar o guarda de dono único: {e}")
    if guard_output.startswith("BLOCK"):
        return refuse("outra sessão viva está numa das branches:\n" + guard_output)

    dirty_files = dirty_tree(repo)
    if dirty_files is None:
        return refuse("não consegui ler o `git status` do clone")
    # The queue lives in the clone and the run itself updates it (`cepa-plan finish`):
    # after every run it is modified. The night branch doesn't touch it, and
    # the merge and the `reset --keep` preserve it.
    clone_queue = (f".claude/queues/{queue}/queue.yaml",
                     f".claude/programs/{queue}/plan.yaml")
    dirty_queue = [l for l in dirty_files if l.endswith(clone_queue)]
    dirty_files = [l for l in dirty_files if l not in dirty_queue]
    if dirty_files:
        return refuse("o clone tem mudança sem commit; um merge só leva "
                      "histórico commitado:\n  " + "\n  ".join(dirty_files[:10]))
    if tree and Path(tree).exists() and dirty_tree(tree):
        return refuse(f"a worktree da noite ({tree}) tem mudança sem commit")

    if not already_merged:
        return_value = head_of(repo)
        landing_info.update({"retorno": return_value, "destino": destination})
        record(aterrissagem=landing_info)
        print(f"\nponto de retorno: `{destination}` em {return_value[:10]}")
        code, output = git(["merge", "--no-ff", "--no-edit", branch], repo)
        if code != 0:
            conflicts = git(["diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=U"],
                            repo)[1].splitlines()
            if conflicts:
                landing_info["parou"] = "conflito"
                record(aterrissagem=landing_info)
                print("CONFLITO no merge, nos arquivos:")
                for c in conflicts:
                    print(f"  {c}")
                print("resolva, `git add`, `git commit` para concluir o merge, "
                      f"e rode `cepa-until aterrissar {a.target} --yes` de novo: "
                      "ele retoma do build")
                return 4
            git(["merge", "--abort"], repo)
            return refuse(f"o merge falhou: {output}")
    landing_info["merge"] = head_of(repo)
    landing_info.pop("parou", None)
    record(aterrissagem=landing_info)

    verify = item_states.get("verify")
    if verify:
        print(f"build completo: {verify}")
        log = path.parent / f"{run_id}.log"
        green, sec, reason = run_verify(verify, repo, 4 * 3600, log)
        if not green:
            return_value = landing_info.get("retorno")
            # Only undoes what this command did: HEAD has to be its merge,
            # with the return point as 1st parent.
            code, first_item = git(["rev-parse", "HEAD^1"], repo)
            if return_value and code == 0 and first_item == return_value:
                # `--keep`, not `--hard`: preserves the queue modified by the run.
                git(["reset", "-q", "--keep", return_value], repo)
                back = f"`{destination}` voltou para {return_value[:10]}"
            else:
                back = (f"`{destination}` NÃO foi desfeito (o HEAD não é o merge "
                         "deste comando); confira à mão")
            landing_info.update({"parou": "build-vermelho", "motivo": reason})
            landing_info.pop("merge", None)
            record(aterrissagem=landing_info)
            print(f"BUILD VERMELHO depois do merge ({reason}): {back}, sem "
                  f"push. A saída está em {log}")
            return 5
        print(f"  verde ({human(timedelta(seconds=sec))})")

    if has_upstream(repo):
        code, output = git(["push"], repo, timeout=300)
        if code != 0:
            landing_info["parou"] = "push"
            record(aterrissagem=landing_info)
            print(f"o push falhou ({output}); o merge e o build verde ficam. "
                  f"Rode `cepa-until aterrissar {a.target} --yes` de novo")
            return 6
        landing_info["push"] = True
        print("push feito")

    if tree and Path(tree).exists():
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(WTLIB), "rescue", tree,
                            branch], capture_output=True, text=True)
        if (r.stdout or "").strip():
            print(r.stdout.strip())
        git(["worktree", "remove", tree], repo)
    code, output = git(["branch", "-d", branch], repo)
    if code != 0:
        print(f"aviso: não apaguei `{branch}` ({output})")
    landing_info["quando"] = datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
    record(estado="aterrissado", aterrissagem=landing_info)
    print(f"aterrissado: `{branch}` está em `{destination}`; worktree e branch da "
          "noite removidas")
    if dirty_queue:
        print(f"a fila ({clone_queue}) tem as marcações do run sem commit; "
              "commite quando quiser")
    return 0


def land_action(repo, tree, queue, run_id, n):
    """The `aterrissar` action of the run's state: the run's normal end and
    `fecha-morto` propose the same one."""
    return {
        "id": "aterrissar",
        "frase": (f"leva os {n} commit(s) da branch da noite para a "
                  f"`{current_branch(repo)}` do clone; só você dispara, porque "
                  "mexe na branch principal"),
        "comando": (f"cepa-until aterrissar {queue}/{run_id} (sem --yes só "
                    "mostra o plano; com --yes faz merge, build completo e "
                    "push)"),
        "sha": head_of(tree), "destino": current_branch(repo),
        "arvore": str(tree)}


# ── decidir: the end of the run asks, instead of just counting ──────────────
#
# The end of the run used to say "14 were deferred (each with its reason, in the report)"
# and "Fica com você: WEGO-2336 (the reason is on each one's line)", and the owner
# was left not knowing what to do with that (09/30). Here every item that only the owner
# unblocks becomes a question, one at a time, and the answer is applied right away.
#
# The ACTIONS stay on a closed list (R2 of
# docs/estrategia-fim-do-cepa-until.md): aterrissar, and `cepa-plan answer`,
# which sends a `blocked` back to the queue or closes the human route with the owner's
# answer. The question text may come from the model's analysis, but it is only shown:
# no wording decides what is executed.

# The generic reason, shown only when the agent did not write the human
# section (`owner_summary.impede`). Until 2026-11-01 it said "travou por algo
# de fora do código" for every blocked item, and on WEGO-2381 that was false:
# the work was done and two rules disagreed.
OWNER_REASON = {
    "bloqueado-antes": "o agente marcou o item como travado",
    "human_pending": "ficou uma tarefa que só você faz",
    "pos-entrega": "o item foi entregue e sobrou uma tarefa que só você faz",
}
NO_OWNER_REASON = {
    "reservado": "outra sessão está nele agora",
    "depende-de-adiado": "depende de um item adiado e anda junto com ele",
}
DECISIONS_BLOCK = re.compile(r"```json cepa-decisoes\s*\n(.*?)\n```", re.S)


def analysis_decisions(text):
    """The ```json cepa-decisoes``` block at the end of `.review.md`: the question and the
    recommendation that /common:until-review wrote for each pending item.
    Used only to SHOW. With no block, or with broken JSON, returns {} and the
    command shows the item's evidence, which is what the agent recorded."""
    m = DECISIONS_BLOCK.search(text or "")
    if not m:
        return {}
    try:
        data = json.loads(m.group(1))
    except ValueError:
        return {}
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        return {}
    items = {}
    for d in data.get("itens") or []:
        if isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("id"):
            items[str(d["id"])] = d
    land_card = data.get("aterrissar")
    return {"aterrissar": land_card if isinstance(land_card, dict) else None,
            "itens": items}


def indented(text, indent="       ", width=96):
    import textwrap
    return textwrap.fill(" ".join(str(text).split()), width=width,
                         initial_indent=indent, subsequent_indent=indent)


def recommendation_line(d):
    if not d or not d.get("recomendo"):
        return None
    return f"Recomendo {d['recomendo']}" + (f": {d['porque']}"
                                           if d.get("porque") else "")


def recommended_letter(d):
    """The menu letter that the analysis recommendation points to: `s` or `n`."""
    r = str((d or {}).get("recomendo") or "").strip().lower()
    return {"sim": "s", "não": "n", "nao": "n"}.get(r)


WORDS_IN_QUESTION = 25


def question_breaks_rules(text):
    """What the question breaks of the human-section rule (up to 25 words;
    no branch, test class, file, card, commit, gate name or verdict; no
    alternative in parentheses), in one sentence, or None. It only warns: the
    question is shown all the same, because it is what the `sim` records
    (decidir WEGO 2026-10-15-1128: 71 words, with branch and class)."""
    return "; ".join(_ownertext.problems(text, WORDS_IN_QUESTION)) or None


def owner_summary_of(ad, d):
    """The human section of a deferred item: what the agent wrote with
    `finish`, completed by the analysis's `se_sim`/`se_nao`. Only text."""
    raw = ad.get("owner_summary")
    summary = {k: " ".join(str(v).split()) for k, v in
               (raw.items() if isinstance(raw, dict) else ())
               if v is not None and str(v).strip()}
    for key in ("se_sim", "se_nao"):
        if not summary.get(key) and str((d or {}).get(key) or "").strip():
            summary[key] = " ".join(str(d[key]).split())
    return summary


def answers_legend(summary):
    """What `sim` and `não` lead to. The mechanics never change (sim returns
    the item to the queue, não keeps it); what the owner needs is what that
    means for the WORK, which only the agent knows (WEGO-2381: "libero o In
    Review?" next to "sim = o item volta para a fila")."""
    yes = summary.get("se_sim")
    no = summary.get("se_nao")
    return (f"sim = {yes or 'o item volta para a fila com a sua resposta'}"
            + (". O item volta para a fila com a sua resposta" if yes else "")
            + f"; não = {no or 'fica como está e eu só gravo o que você disser'}")


def pending_action(item_states):
    """The `aterrissar` action of the state, if it still needs doing. `aterrissar`
    records `aterrissado` in the state and leaves the action in the list, as a record."""
    if (item_states or {}).get("estado") == "aterrissado":
        return None
    return next((x for x in (item_states or {}).get("acoes") or []
                 if isinstance(x, dict) and x.get("id") == "aterrissar"), None)


def is_yes(r):
    return str(r or "").strip().lower() in ("s", "sim", "y", "yes")


class NoAnswer(TimeoutError):
    """Nobody typed within the wait."""


def read_line(prompt, output=print, wait=None):
    """`input()` that doesn't die on an unreadable line. A dead-key accent
    half-erased arrives as a stray byte (`n\\xcb\\xc3\\xa3o`) and
    `input()` blows up with UnicodeDecodeError; the line was already consumed, so
    just ask again (decidir WEGO 2026-09-29-2059)."""
    while True:
        try:
            if wait is not None:
                sys.stdout.write(prompt)
                sys.stdout.flush()
                if not select.select([sys.stdin], [], [], wait)[0]:
                    raise NoAnswer(f"no answer in {wait}s")
                return input("")
            return input(prompt)
        except UnicodeDecodeError:
            output("       não consegui ler essa linha (algum acento chegou "
                  "pela metade); digite de novo")


class Panel:
    """How the end-of-run questions appear. Outside a terminal (tests,
    `nohup`, agent) the text is byte for byte the old one: label, colon,
    7-space indent. On a terminal each question becomes a card with a left
    border, labels dimmed in a single column, the question in bold, the
    recommendation in color and the menu in chips with the recommended key in green.
    The phrases that the keys answer (`Aterrisso agora?`, `[t] escrevo a
    resposta`, `Quer acrescentar algo`) stay whole in a single color: it is
    by them that the pty tests know when to answer."""

    LABEL_WIDTH = 14

    def __init__(self, screen, output):
        self.t = screen
        self.enabled = screen.enabled
        self.output = output

    # ── primitives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    def _w(self):
        return self.t.width()

    def _wrap(self, text, indent, hanging=None):
        import textwrap
        hanging = indent if hanging is None else hanging
        text = " ".join(str(text).split())
        return textwrap.wrap(text, width=self._w(),
                             initial_indent=" " * indent,
                             subsequent_indent=" " * hanging,
                             break_on_hyphens=False) or [" " * indent]

    def _border(self, line="", color=None):
        """`│  text` with a dimmed border; `line` already comes indented."""
        body = self.t.c(color, line) if color else line
        self.output(self.t.c("cinza", "│") + body)

    def _top(self, label, color="magenta"):
        rest = max(self._w() - len(label) - 4, 0)
        self.output(self.t.c(color, "┌─ ") + self.t.c("negrito", label) + " "
                   + self.t.c(color, "─" * rest))

    def _prompt(self, text):
        """The `input()` prompt, inside the card."""
        if not self.enabled:
            return text
        return self.t.c("cinza", "│  ") + self.t.c("negrito", text)

    def end(self):
        """Closes the card. Outside a terminal it doesn't exist."""
        if self.enabled:
            self.output(self.t.c("cinza", "└─"))

    # ── opening and closing ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    def nothing(self):
        if self.enabled:
            self.output("")
            self.output(self.t.rule("nada espera por você neste run"))
        else:
            self.output("\n── nada espera por você neste run")

    def open_panel(self, total):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(f"\n── {total} pergunta(s) para você. Uma por vez: s ou n "
                       "basta; Enter deixa para depois, q encerra")
            return
        self.output("")
        self.output(self.t.rule(f"{total} pergunta(s) para você"))
        self.output("   " + self.t.c("cinza", "uma por vez · s ou n basta · Enter "
                                             "deixa para depois · q encerra"))

    def close_panel(self, without_owner, applied, for_later, back):
        t = self.t
        if not self.enabled:
            if without_owner:
                self.output(f"\n   Não dependem de você ({len(without_owner)}): "
                           + "; ".join(without_owner))
            self.output(f"\n   Respondido agora: {len(applied)} · para depois: "
                       f"{len(for_later)}")
            for x in applied:
                self.output(f"     ✓ {x}")
            if for_later:
                self.output(f"   Para voltar a estas perguntas: {back}")
            return
        self.output("")
        self.output(t.rule("fecho"))
        if without_owner:
            for l in self._wrap(f"Não dependem de você ({len(without_owner)}): "
                                  + "; ".join(without_owner), 3):
                self.output(t.c("cinza", l))
        self.output("   " + t.c("verde", f"respondido agora {len(applied)}")
                   + t.c("cinza", " · ")
                   + t.c("amarelo" if for_later else "cinza",
                         f"para depois {len(for_later)}"))
        for x in applied:
            self.output("     " + t.c("verde", "✓ ") + x)
        if for_later:
            self.output("   " + t.c("cinza", "para voltar a estas perguntas: ")
                       + t.c("ciano", back))

    # ── aterrissar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    def land_card(self, phrase, rec):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(f"\n   Aterrissar: {phrase}")
            if rec:
                self.output(indented(rec, "   "))
            return "   Aterrisso agora? [s/N/q] "
        self.output("")
        self._top("aterrissar")
        for l in self._wrap(phrase, 2):
            self._border(l)
        if rec:
            self.recommend(rec)
        return self._prompt("Aterrisso agora? [s/N/q] ")

    # ── one item ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    def item(self, i, n, ident, title):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(f"\n   ━━ [{i}/{n}] {ident}")
            self.output(indented(title, "   "))
            self.output("")
            return
        self.output("")
        self._top(f"{i}/{n} · {ident}", "ciano")
        for l in self._wrap(title, 2):
            self._border(l, "negrito")
        self._border()

    def label(self, name, text, short_path=None):
        """`name: text` outside a terminal; on a terminal the label (or its
        `short`) goes in a dimmed column and the text aligns beside it."""
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(f"{name}: {text}"))
            return
        tag = f"  {(short_path or name):<{self.LABEL_WIDTH}} "
        lines = self._wrap(text, len(tag))
        self._border(self.t.c("cinza", tag) + lines[0][len(tag):])
        for l in lines[1:]:
            self._border(l)

    def blank(self):
        self.output("") if not self.enabled else self._border()

    def question(self, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(f"Pergunta: {text}"))
            return
        lines = self._wrap(text, 4)
        self._border("  " + self.t.c("amarelo", "?") + " "
                    + self.t.c("negrito", lines[0][4:]))
        for l in lines[1:]:
            self._border(self.t.c("negrito", l))

    def warning(self, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(text))
            return
        for l in self._wrap(text, 4):
            self._border(l, "amarelo")

    def note(self, text):
        """Support line for the question (`Se sim, o próximo run recebe`)."""
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(text))
            return
        for l in self._wrap(text, 4):
            self._border(l, "cinza")

    def recommend(self, rec):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(rec))
            return
        head_of, _, rest = rec.partition(": ")
        color = "verde" if head_of.endswith("sim") else "amarelo"
        lines = self._wrap(rec, 4, 4)
        self._border("  " + self.t.c(color, "✦ " + lines[0][4:]))
        for l in lines[1:]:
            self._border(l, color)

    def legend(self, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(text))
            return
        for l in self._wrap(text, 2):
            self._border(l, "cinza")

    def menu(self, chips, recommended):
        """`chips` is the list of (key, label); returns the `input()`
        prompt. Outside a terminal it is the old line, whole in the prompt."""
        parts = []
        for key, lbl in chips:
            mark = " (recomendado)" if key == recommended else ""
            parts.append(f"[{key}] {lbl}{mark}")
        if not self.enabled:
            return "       " + " · ".join(parts) + ": "
        sep = self.t.c("cinza", " · ")
        color = {recommended: "verde"}
        painted_items = [self.t.c("negrito", self.t.c(color.get(k, "ciano"), p))
                    for (k, _), p in zip(chips, parts)]
        # The chips fit in the width; what is left over drops to the next line.
        lines, current, spent = [], [], 0
        for raw_text, painted in zip(parts, painted_items):
            if current and spent + 3 + len(raw_text) > self._w() - 3:
                lines.append(current)
                current, spent = [], 0
            current.append(painted)
            spent += len(raw_text) + (3 if len(current) > 1 else 0)
        lines.append(current)
        self._border()
        for l in lines:
            self._border("  " + sep.join(l))
        return self._prompt("▸ ")

    def follow_up(self, text):
        """Prompt of a support question inside the card."""
        if not self.enabled:
            return f"       {text}"
        return self.t.c("cinza", "│  ") + text

    def key_error(self, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(f"       {text}")
        else:
            self._border("  " + self.t.c("vermelho", text))

    def evidence(self, text):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(indented(f"Detalhe técnico (para agentes): {text}"))
            return
        self.label("Detalhe técnico", text, short_path="Para agentes")

    def recorded(self, msg, ok=True):
        if not self.enabled:
            self.output(f"       → {msg}" if ok else f"       → não gravei: {msg}")
            return
        self._border("  " + (self.t.c("verde", f"✓ {msg}") if ok
                            else self.t.c("vermelho", f"✗ não gravei: {msg}")))


def decide(repo, queue, run_id, item_states, deferred, analysis, question=None,
           output=print, answer=None, land=None, wait=None):
    """Goes through what only the owner unblocks and applies each answer. Returns
    (applied, for_later), as text, for the closing."""
    if question is None:
        def question(prompt):
            return read_line(prompt, output, wait)
    analysis = analysis or {}
    by_item = analysis.get("itens") or {}
    if answer is None:
        def answer(ident, text, keep=False, drop=False):
            p = subprocess.run(
                [sys.executable, str(CEPA_PLAN), "answer", queue, ident,
                 "--answer", text, "--repo", str(repo)]
                + (["--keep"] if keep else [])
                + (["--drop"] if drop else []),
                capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            return p.returncode, (p.stdout or p.stderr).strip()
    if land is None:
        def land():
            return cmd_land([f"{queue}/{run_id}", "--repo", str(repo),
                                   "--yes"])
    back = f"cepa-until decide {queue}" + (f"/{run_id}" if run_id else "")
    screen = Panel(SCREEN, output)
    applied, for_later = [], []
    owner_items = [ad for ad in deferred if ad.get("reason") in OWNER_REASON]
    without_owner = [ad for ad in deferred if ad.get("reason") in NO_OWNER_REASON]
    action = pending_action(item_states)
    total = (1 if action else 0) + len(owner_items)
    if not total:
        screen.nothing()
        return applied, for_later

    screen.open_panel(total)
    stopped = False

    if action:
        prompt = screen.land_card(action.get("frase"),
                                 recommendation_line(analysis.get("aterrissar")))
        r = question(prompt)
        if str(r).strip().lower() == "q":
            stopped = True
        elif is_yes(r):
            rc = land()
            (applied if rc == 0 else for_later).append(
                "aterrissar" + ("" if rc == 0 else
                                f" (parou com código {rc}; a saída está acima)"))
        if not is_yes(r):
            for_later.append(f"aterrissar: cepa-until aterrissar "
                               f"{queue}/{run_id} --yes")
        screen.end()

    for i, ad in enumerate(owner_items, 1):
        ident = str(ad.get("id"))
        if stopped:
            for_later.append(f"{ident}: {OWNER_REASON[ad['reason']]}")
            continue
        d = by_item.get(ident) or {}
        route = ad.get("human_pending")
        question_text = ad.get("question") or d.get("pergunta")
        instruction = " ".join(str(d.get("instrucao") or "").split())
        context = " ".join(str(d.get("contexto") or "").split())
        # One block per item, with each part under its label and a blank line
        # between context, question and menu. Whole title: cut at 60
        # characters the owner answered a question he saw only half of
        # (feedback of 10/15, decidir WEGO 2026-10-15-1128).
        summary = owner_summary_of(ad, d)
        screen.item(i, len(owner_items), ident, ad.get("title") or "")
        # The human section first, in the order a person reads a story:
        # what stopped, what was asked, what is already done. The agent
        # section (the evidence, with its codes) only on `[e]`.
        screen.label("Parou porque", summary.get("impede")
                     or f"{OWNER_REASON[ad['reason']]}.")
        if summary.get("pedido"):
            screen.label("Era para", summary["pedido"])
        if summary.get("pronto"):
            screen.label("Já está pronto", summary["pronto"])
        if route is not None:
            screen.label("Tarefa que ficou para você", route, short_path="Tarefa")
        if context:
            screen.label("Contexto", context)
        # A single question, and `sim` always means the same thing: the item
        # goes back to the queue. The old menu ([r]/[f]/[m]) had no "sim",
        # even though the question ended in "Recomendo sim" (feedback of
        # 10/15: "99% of the time I don't know what to answer"). With no written
        # question, the terminal asks the default one, instead of showing the evidence and
        # leaving the owner to find the question on his own.
        screen.blank()
        if question_text:
            screen.question(question_text)
            outside = question_breaks_rules(question_text)
            if outside:
                screen.warning(f"(esta pergunta foi escrita fora das "
                           f"regras: {outside}. Se ela não fizer sentido, "
                           "[e] mostra o detalhe técnico)")
        elif route is not None and ad.get("reason") == "pos-entrega":
            screen.question("já fez? Com sim, a tarefa fecha; o item segue "
                          "concluído.")
        elif route is not None:
            screen.question("já fez? Com sim, a tarefa fecha e o item volta "
                          "para a fila.")
        elif summary.get("impede"):
            screen.question("destravo o item e devolvo para a fila?")
        else:
            screen.label("O agente parou porque",
                        summarize_reason(ad.get('evidence') or ''),
                        short_path="Evidência")
            screen.question("destravo o item e devolvo para a fila?")
        if instruction:
            screen.note(f"Se sim, o próximo run recebe: {instruction}")
        rec = recommendation_line(d)
        if rec:
            screen.recommend(rec)
        screen.blank()
        screen.legend("sim = a tarefa fecha; não = continua aberta; d = ela "
                      "não vale mais e fecha sem ter sido feita"
                      if ad.get("reason") == "pos-entrega"
                      else answers_legend(summary) + "; d = o item sai da fila")
        show = bool(ad.get("evidence"))
        delivered = ad.get("reason") == "pos-entrega"
        # `d` exists because "sim" always means "back to the queue": on
        # 2026-11-02 the owner said sim to "descarto este pedido?" (WEGO-2463)
        # and the item went back to `pending`, for the next run to redo.
        chips = [("s", "sim"), ("n", "não"), ("t", "escrevo a resposta"),
                 ("d", "a tarefa não vale mais" if delivered
                  else "descarta o item")]
        if show:
            chips.append(("e", "detalhe técnico"))
        chips += [("Enter", "depois"), ("q", "encerra")]
        prompt = screen.menu(chips, recommended_letter(d))
        valid = {"s", "n", "t", "d", "", "q"} | ({"e"} if show else set())
        while True:
            raw = str(question(prompt))
            r = raw.strip().lower()
            r = {"sim": "s", "yes": "s", "y": "s",
                 "não": "n", "nao": "n", "no": "n"}.get(r, r)
            if r == "e" and show:
                screen.evidence(ad.get("evidence"))
                continue
            if r not in valid:
                # Loose text here used to go to later silently, and the answer
                # the owner wrote vanished (decidir WEGO 2026-09-29-2059).
                screen.key_error(f"\"{raw.strip()}\" não é uma das opções; "
                                   "para escrever uma resposta, digite t primeiro")
                continue
            break
        if r == "q":
            stopped = True
        text, give_back, drop = "", False, False
        if r == "d":
            drop = True
            base = question_text or route or "o item"
            extra = str(question(screen.follow_up(
                "Por quê, numa linha? [Enter pula] "))).strip()
            text = (("tarefa encerrada" if delivered else "descartado")
                    + f": {base}" + (f". {extra}" if extra else ""))
        elif r == "t":
            text = str(question(screen.follow_up("Sua resposta, numa linha (o "
                                               "próximo run lê isto): "))).strip()
            if text:
                give_back = is_yes(question(screen.follow_up(
                    "Devolvo o item para a fila com essa resposta? [s/N] ")))
        elif r in ("s", "n"):
            give_back = r == "s"
            base = question_text or route or "destravar o item"
            # There is always room for a comment, also on `s` with a
            # written question: the owner wanted to say something beyond yes/no and
            # the next run reads what he wrote (10/15).
            extra = str(question(screen.follow_up(
                "Quer acrescentar algo, numa linha? [Enter pula] "))).strip()
            text = (("sim" if give_back else "não") + f": {base}"
                     + (f" Instrução: {instruction}" if give_back and instruction
                        else "")
                     + (f". {extra}" if extra else ""))
        if text:
            rc, msg = (answer(ident, text, drop=True) if drop
                       else answer(ident, text) if give_back
                       else answer(ident, text, keep=True))
            if rc == 0:
                applied.append(f"{ident}: {msg}")
                screen.recorded(msg)
                screen.end()
                continue
            screen.recorded(msg, ok=False)
        for_later.append(f"{ident}: {OWNER_REASON[ad['reason']]}")
        screen.end()

    screen.close_panel([f"{ad.get('id')} ({NO_OWNER_REASON[ad['reason']]})"
                for ad in without_owner], applied, for_later,
               back)
    return applied, for_later


def pending_as_text(queue, run_id, item_states, deferred, analysis, output=print):
    """Without a terminal (the run launched by `nohup`, or read by another program):
    the same list, without asking."""
    analysis = analysis or {}
    by_item = analysis.get("itens") or {}
    action = pending_action(item_states)
    owner_items = [ad for ad in deferred if ad.get("reason") in OWNER_REASON]
    if not action and not owner_items:
        return
    output(f"\n── esperam por você: {(1 if action else 0) + len(owner_items)}")
    if action:
        output(f"   - aterrissar: {action.get('frase')}")
    for ad in owner_items:
        d = by_item.get(str(ad.get("id"))) or {}
        q = ad.get("question") or d.get("pergunta") or ad.get("human_pending") \
            or summarize_reason(ad.get("evidence") or "")
        why = owner_summary_of(ad, d).get("impede") or OWNER_REASON[ad["reason"]]
        output(f"   - {ad.get('id')} ({why}): {q}")
    output(f"   Para responder uma por uma, num terminal: cepa-until decide "
          f"{queue}" + (f"/{run_id}" if run_id else ""))


def delivered_leftovers(queue, repo):
    """The `done` items that still carry a `human_pending`: delivered work with
    a task only the owner does (create a role, validate by hand). No run asks
    about them, so on 2026-11-02 the WEGO queue had 37 of them and the owner
    had to know `cepa-plan answer` to close each one."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(
            [sys.executable, str(CEPA_PLAN), "status", queue, "--status", "done",
             "--repo", str(repo), "--json"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        items = json.loads(p.stdout).get("items") or [] if p.returncode == 0 else []
    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError):
        items = []
    return [{"id": l.get("id"), "title": l.get("title"), "reason": "pos-entrega",
             "question": None, "human_pending": l.get("human_pending"),
             "owner_summary": l.get("owner_summary"),
             "evidence": l.get("evidence")}
            for l in items if l.get("human_pending") is not None]


def close_with_owner(repo, queue, run_id, item_states, review=None, interactive=None,
                     wait=None):
    """The closing of the run and of `cepa-until decide`: queries the queue again (its
    state now, not the launch one) and asks, or lists without a terminal.
    Without `run_id` (`cepa-until decide <fila>`), it goes over the whole queue:
    every deferred item plus the leftover tasks of the delivered ones."""
    data, error = query_queue(queue, repo)
    if error:
        print(f"\n── não consegui listar os adiados ({error})")
        deferred = []
    else:
        deferred = (data or {}).get("deferred") or []
    if not run_id:
        deferred = deferred + delivered_leftovers(queue, repo)
    analysis = {}
    if review:
        try:
            analysis = analysis_decisions(
                Path(review).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except OSError:
            analysis = {}
    if interactive is None:
        interactive = sys.stdin.isatty() and sys.stdout.isatty()
    if not interactive:
        pending_as_text(queue, run_id, item_states, deferred, analysis)
        return 0
    try:
        decide(repo, queue, run_id, item_states, deferred, analysis, wait=wait)
    except NoAnswer:
        print(f"\n   ninguém respondeu em {wait / 60:g} min; o run termina aqui. "
              f"Para responder depois: cepa-until decide {queue}"
              + (f"/{run_id}" if run_id else ""))
    except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):
        print("\n   perguntas interrompidas; volte com: cepa-until decide "
              f"{queue}" + (f"/{run_id}" if run_id else ""))
    return 0


def cmd_decide(argv):
    """`cepa-until decide <queue>/<run>`: the end-of-run questions, again,
    for when the owner wasn't there or left some for later.
    `cepa-until decide <queue>`: every question the queue holds for the owner,
    from any run, including the leftover tasks of delivered items (owner,
    2026-11-02: "eu odeio ter que usar qualquer outro comando cepa que não seja
    o cepa-until")."""
    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa until decide",
        summary=_sub_summary("decide"),
        description=(
            "The end-of-run questions again, for when the owner was not there or\n"
            "left some for later. With <queue>, everything the queue holds for the\n"
            "owner, from any run, including the leftover tasks of delivered items.\n"
            "With <queue>/<run>, the landing (aterrissar) and each deferred item of\n"
            "that run.\n"
            "\n"
            "Each question is closed, with a recommendation, and the answer is\n"
            "applied right away (cepa plan answer). Outside a terminal it prints\n"
            "the pending questions as text instead of asking."),
        examples=[
            ("cepa until decide wego", "every question the queue holds for you"),
            ("cepa until decide wego/2026-11-03-2210", "the questions of one run"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "questions asked or listed (also when interrupted or unanswered)"),
            (2, "invalid usage, invalid queue or run name, queue or run state "
                "unreadable"),
        ],
        see_also=["cepa until pendentes: which runs are waiting for you",
                  "cepa plan answer: what applies each answer"])
    ap.add_argument("target", metavar="QUEUE[/RUN]",
                    help="the whole queue, or one run as the run summary prints it")
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=".", metavar="DIR",
                    help="repository root (default: the current directory)")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if "/" not in a.target:
        if not (re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", a.target)
                and ".." not in a.target):
            print(f"cepa-until decide: fila inválida {a.target!r}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        repo = Path(a.repo).resolve()
        _, error = query_queue(a.target, repo)
        if error:
            print(f"cepa-until decide: não li a fila {a.target!r} ({error})",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return close_with_owner(repo, a.target, None, {})
    queue, run_id = a.target.split("/", 1)
    # Queue and run names are a single segment: `queue/../../x` would read a
    # state from outside the run folder and ask about it.
    if not all(re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", x) and ".." not in x
               for x in (queue, run_id)):
        print(f"cepa-until decide: alvo inválido {a.target!r}; é <fila>/<run>, "
              "sem barras nem `..` dentro de cada parte", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    repo = Path(a.repo).resolve()
    folder = qp.queue_dir(repo, queue) / "until"
    try:
        item_states = json.loads((folder / f"{run_id}.estado.json").read_text(
            encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"cepa-until decide: não li o estado do run em {folder} ({e})",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    review = folder / f"{run_id}.review.md"
    return close_with_owner(repo, queue, run_id, item_states,
                            review if review.exists() else None)


def cmd_close_dead(argv):
    """`cepa-until fecha-morto <queue>/<run> [--yes]` — closes the run whose
    supervisor died (or was interrupted) before the end.

    Run WEGO 2026-09-28-2003 stopped at `item_start`: the card closed `done`
    on its own and the full build the supervisor runs after each `done`
    never ran. The state stayed `rodando`, and `aterrissar` only accepts
    `esperando-dono`. This command does what the supervisor didn't: it runs the
    full build in the night worktree and, if green, records `run_end` and leaves the
    run `esperando-dono` with the `aterrissar` action. If red, it doesn't change the state:
    `cepa-doctor` keeps pointing at the run. Without `--yes`, it only shows the plan."""
    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa until fecha-morto",
        summary=_sub_summary("fecha-morto"),
        description=(
            "Closes a run whose supervisor died (or was interrupted) before the\n"
            "end: the state stayed `rodando`, with no `run_end`, and the full build\n"
            "the supervisor runs after each `done` item never ran. This command runs\n"
            "that build in the run worktree (recreating it from the run branch if it\n"
            "is gone).\n"
            "\n"
            "Green: it records `run_end` and leaves the run waiting for the owner,\n"
            "ready for aterrissar. Red: nothing changes, and cepa doctor keeps\n"
            "pointing at the run. It refuses while the supervisor or the child\n"
            "process of the item in flight is still alive.\n"
            "Without --yes, it only shows the plan."),
        examples=[
            ("cepa until fecha-morto wego/2026-09-28-2003", "show the closing plan"),
            ("cepa until fecha-morto wego/2026-09-28-2003 --yes", "run the missing build"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "run closed (green build), or plan shown (without --yes)"),
            (1, "the build is red: the state did not change"),
            (2, "invalid usage, target not <queue>/<run>, or run state unreadable"),
            (3, "refused: the run is not dead (finished, supervisor or child alive, "
                "cannot tell), or its worktree is not recorded, cannot be recreated "
                "or is dirty"),
        ],
        see_also=["cepa until pendentes: lists the dead runs",
                  "cepa doctor: points at a dead run"])
    ap.add_argument("target", metavar="QUEUE/RUN",
                    help="the dead run, as cepa doctor prints it")
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=".", metavar="DIR",
                    help="repository root (default: the current directory)")
    ap.add_argument("--yes", "--sim", dest="yes", action="store_true",
                    help="executes; without it, only shows the plan")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)

    def refuse(text):
        print(f"cepa-until fecha-morto: {text}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    if "/" not in a.target:
        print("cepa-until fecha-morto: o alvo é <fila>/<run> (ex.: "
              "wego/2026-09-28-2003)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    queue, run_id = a.target.split("/", 1)
    repo = main_root(Path(a.repo).resolve())
    path = qp.queue_dir(repo, queue) / "until" / \
        f"{run_id}.estado.json"
    try:
        item_states = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"cepa-until fecha-morto: não li o estado do run em {path} "
              f"({e})", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    m = next((x for x in dead_runs(repo)
              if x.get("fila") == queue and x.get("run") == run_id), None)
    if not m:
        if item_states.get("estado") not in ("rodando", "interrompido"):
            return refuse(f"o run {run_id} está `{item_states.get('estado')}`: ele "
                          "chegou ao fim, e não há o que fechar")
        pid = item_states.get("pid")
        if pid and supervisor_alive(pid):
            return refuse(f"o supervisor do run {run_id} está vivo (pid {pid} "
                          f"em {item_states.get('host')}); espere o fim dele")
        return refuse(f"não consigo dizer que o supervisor do run {run_id} "
                      "morreu (pid de outra máquina, ou run sem pid ainda "
                      "dentro do prazo), ou a branch da noite já entrou "
                      "ou sumiu")
    child = (item_states.get("item_em_voo") or {}).get("pid_filho")
    if child:
        try:
            os.killpg(int(child), 0)
            return refuse(f"o processo filho do item em voo (pid {child}) "
                          "ainda roda; espere ele acabar ou encerre-o")
        except (ProcessLookupError, ValueError, TypeError):
            pass
        except OSError:
            pass
    tree, branch, verify = m.get("arvore"), m.get("branch"), m.get("verify")
    if not tree:
        return refuse("o run não gravou a worktree da noite")
    tree = Path(tree)
    recreate = not tree.is_dir()

    print(f"fechar o run {run_id} da fila {queue} ({m['como']})")
    if m.get("item"):
        print(f"  item em voo: {m['item']}, status `{m.get('status')}`")
    print(f"  worktree   : {tree}"
          + (f" (sumiu; recrio a partir de `{branch}`)" if recreate else ""))
    print(f"  build      : {verify or 'nenhum (o run dispensou o build)'}")
    print("  verde      : grava `run_end` e deixa o run `esperando-dono` com a "
          "ação `aterrissar`")
    print("  vermelho   : não muda nada; o doctor segue apontando o run")
    if not a.yes:
        print(f"\nnada foi feito. Para executar: cepa-until fecha-morto "
              f"{a.target} --yes")
        return 0

    if recreate:
        git(["worktree", "prune"], repo)
        c, error = git(["worktree", "add", str(tree), str(branch)], repo)
        if c != 0:
            return refuse(f"não recriei a worktree da noite: {error}")
    dirty_files = dirty_tree(tree)
    if dirty_files:
        return refuse("a worktree da noite tem mudança sem commit; o build "
                      "mediria o que não vai para a branch. Commite ou guarde "
                      "antes:\n  " + "\n  ".join(dirty_files[:10]))

    record_path = Path(m["registro"])

    def log_event(event):
        event["quando"] = datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
        with record_path.open("a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")

    if verify:
        print(f"\nbuild completo: {verify}")
        green, sec, reason = run_verify(verify, tree, 4 * 3600,
                                         record_path.with_suffix(".log"))
        log_event({"evento": "verify", "id": m.get("item"), "verde": green,
                  "segundos": int(sec), "motivo": reason, "fechamento": True})
        if not green:
            print(f"vermelho ({reason}). O estado não mudou; a saída está em "
                  f"{short_path(record_path.with_suffix('.log'), repo)}")
            return 1
        print(f"verde em {human(timedelta(seconds=int(sec)))}")

    base = m.get("base")
    c, n = git(["rev-list", "--count", f"{base}..HEAD"], tree)
    n = int(n) if c == 0 and n.isdigit() else -1
    reason = ("interrompido" if item_states.get("estado") == "interrompido"
              else "supervisor-morto")
    log_event({"evento": "run_end", "motivo": reason,
              "detalhe": f"fechado pelo fecha-morto ({m['como']})",
              "fechado_por": "fecha-morto", "item_em_voo": m.get("item")})
    stays = []
    if m.get("item") and m.get("status") != "done":
        stays.append({"id": m["item"], "texto": (
            f"ficou `{m.get('status')}` quando o supervisor morreu; o próximo "
            "run o retoma pela reserva órfã")})
    actions = [] if n == 0 else [land_action(repo, tree, queue, run_id,
                                               n if n > 0 else "?")]
    item_states.update(estado="esperando-dono" if actions or stays else "encerrado",
               motivo_fim=reason, acoes=actions, fica_com_voce=stays,
               fechado_por="fecha-morto",
               atualizado=datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"))
    tmp = path.parent / (path.name + ".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(item_states, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n",
                   encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, path)
    if actions:
        print(f"o run está `esperando-dono`. Próximo passo: "
              f"{actions[0]['comando']}")
    else:
        print(f"o run está `{item_states['estado']}` (a branch da noite não tem "
              "commit sobre a largada)")
    return 0


def short_path(path, repo):
    """Path to read on screen (A6): relative to the repo when it is inside
    it, `~/...` when it is in the home, and whole only for the rest."""
    c = Path(path)
    for base, prefix in ((Path(repo), ""), (Path.home(), "~/")):
        for b in (base, base.resolve()):
            try:
                return prefix + str(c.relative_to(b))
            except ValueError:
                continue
    return str(c)


def main_root(repo):
    """The main clone of `repo` (from a worktree, the clone that owns it): it is there
    that the queues and the run records live."""
    code, common_dir = git(["rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute",
                         "--git-common-dir"], repo)
    if code != 0:
        return Path(repo).resolve()
    common_dir = Path(common_dir)
    return common_dir.parent if common_dir.name == ".git" else common_dir


def run_states(root):
    """Every run `*.estado.json`, in both layouts, in path order."""
    found = []
    for base in (qp.LEGACY_DIR, qp.NEW_DIR):
        found.extend((Path(root) / base).glob("*/until/*.estado.json"))
    return sorted(found)


def waiting_runs(repo):
    """The runs whose `aterrissar` action is still valid: state `esperando-dono`,
    night branch existing and still outside the destination branch. A merge done
    by hand, outside `aterrissar`, also takes the run off the list."""
    root = main_root(repo)
    found = []
    for path in run_states(root):
        try:
            item_states = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if not isinstance(item_states, dict) or item_states.get("estado") != "esperando-dono":
            continue
        action = next((x for x in item_states.get("acoes") or []
                     if isinstance(x, dict) and x.get("id") == "aterrissar"),
                    None)
        if not action:
            continue
        code, sha = git(["rev-parse", "--verify", "-q",
                           str(item_states.get("branch"))], root)
        if code != 0:
            continue
        destination = action.get("destino") or current_branch(root)
        code, _ = git(["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", sha, destination], root)
        if code == 0:
            continue
        queue, run = item_states.get("fila"), item_states.get("run")
        found.append({"fila": queue, "run": run, "branch": item_states.get("branch"),
                        "destino": destination,
                        "fica_com_voce": len(item_states.get("fica_com_voce") or []),
                        "comando": f"cepa-until aterrissar {queue}/{run}"})
    return found


def supervisor_alive(pid):
    """Is the pid still a `cepa-until` on this machine? `ps` tells the live
    supervisor apart from a pid recycled by another process."""
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return True
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(int(pid))],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return True
    if p.returncode != 0 and not p.stdout.strip():
        return False
    return "cepa-until" in p.stdout


def dead_runs(repo, now=None):
    """The runs with state `rodando` whose supervisor died without closing the
    record. The case that paid for this (WEGO 2026-09-28-2003): the `.jsonl`
    stopped at `item_start`, the card closed `done` on its own and the full build that
    the supervisor runs after each `done` never ran. The pid only holds on the
    machine that recorded it; a run without a pid (before 2026-09-29) counts as
    dead when the deadline passed more than `MARGIN_WITHOUT_PID` ago. A run whose
    night branch has already entered the clone's branch or vanished leaves the list."""
    now = now or datetime.now()
    root = main_root(repo)
    host = socket.gethostname()
    found = []
    for path in run_states(root):
        try:
            item_states = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if not isinstance(item_states, dict) or item_states.get("estado") not in (
                "rodando", "interrompido"):
            continue
        record_path = path.parent / (item_states.get("registro") or path.name.replace(
            ".estado.json", ".jsonl"))
        events = []
        try:
            for line in record_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
                try:
                    events.append(json.loads(line))
                except ValueError:
                    continue
        except OSError:
            pass
        start = next((e for e in events if e.get("evento") == "run_start"),
                      {})
        pid = item_states.get("pid") or start.get("pid")
        owner = item_states.get("host") or start.get("host")
        if item_states.get("estado") == "interrompido":
            how = (f"interrompido por {item_states.get('sinal') or 'um sinal'}, sem o "
                    "fim normal")
        elif pid:
            if owner and owner != host:
                continue
            if supervisor_alive(pid):
                continue
            how = f"o supervisor (pid {pid}) não existe mais em {host}"
        else:
            try:
                deadline = datetime.fromisoformat(str(start.get("prazo")))
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if now < deadline + MARGIN_WITHOUT_PID:
                continue
            how = (f"o run não grava o pid do supervisor e o prazo "
                    f"({deadline.strftime('%d/%m %H:%M')}) passou há "
                    f"{human(now - deadline)}")
        branch = item_states.get("branch") or start.get("branch")
        code, sha = git(["rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", str(branch)], root)
        if code != 0:
            continue
        code, _ = git(["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", sha, "HEAD"], root)
        if code == 0:
            continue
        in_flight = None
        for e in events:
            if e.get("evento") == "item_start":
                in_flight = e.get("id")
            elif e.get("evento") == "item_end":
                in_flight = None
        queue = item_states.get("fila") or start.get("fila")
        status = None
        if in_flight:
            it, _ = read_item(qp.queue_file(root, str(queue)), in_flight)
            status = str((it or {}).get("status") or "?")
        tree = item_states.get("arvore") or start.get("arvore")
        verify = item_states.get("verify") if "verify" in item_states else start.get("verify")
        command = None
        if verify and tree:
            command = f"cd {shlex.quote(tree)} && {verify}"
            if not Path(tree).is_dir():
                command = (f"git -C {shlex.quote(str(root))} worktree add "
                           f"{shlex.quote(tree)} {branch} && " + command)
        found.append({"fila": queue, "run": item_states.get("run"), "branch": branch,
                        "estado": item_states.get("estado"),
                        "como": how, "item": in_flight, "status": status,
                        "arvore": tree, "verify": verify,
                        "comando": command,
                        "fechar": f"cepa-until fecha-morto {queue}/"
                                  f"{item_states.get('run')}",
                        "estado_json": str(path), "registro": str(record_path),
                        "base": start.get("base")})
    return found


def live_run_of_queue(repo, queue):
    """The run of this queue that is up right now, or None. State `rodando`, pid
    of a live `cepa-until`, on this machine. A run from another host can't be
    checked from here and counts as not alive (same rule as `dead_runs`); a
    run without a pid too, because without a pid there is no way to tell live from dead.
    Returns `{run, pid, prazo, estado_json, iniciados}`, with `iniciados` the
    ids of the items with `item_start` in the run's record."""
    root = main_root(repo)
    host = socket.gethostname()
    folder = qp.queue_dir(root, str(queue)) / "until"
    for path in sorted(folder.glob("*.estado.json")):
        try:
            item_states = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if not isinstance(item_states, dict) or item_states.get("estado") != "rodando":
            continue
        record_path = folder / (item_states.get("registro") or path.name.replace(
            ".estado.json", ".jsonl"))
        events = []
        try:
            for line in record_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
                try:
                    events.append(json.loads(line))
                except ValueError:
                    continue
        except OSError:
            pass
        start = next((e for e in events if e.get("evento") == "run_start"),
                      {})
        pid = item_states.get("pid") or start.get("pid")
        owner = item_states.get("host") or start.get("host")
        if not pid or (owner and owner != host) or not supervisor_alive(pid):
            continue
        return {"run": item_states.get("run"), "pid": pid,
                "prazo": item_states.get("prazo") or start.get("prazo"),
                "estado_json": str(path),
                "iniciados": {str(e.get("id")) for e in events
                              if e.get("evento") == "item_start"}}
    return None


def dead_run_phrase(m):
    """One line for the run whose supervisor died: `pendentes` and
    `cepa-doctor` say the same thing."""
    item = ""
    if m.get("item"):
        item = (f"; o item em voo, {m['item']}, está `{m.get('status')}`"
                + (" sem o build completo que o supervisor roda depois de "
                   "cada done" if m.get("status") == "done" else ""))
    offer = (f" — o build completo que faltou: {m['comando']}"
              if m.get("comando") else
              " — o run não tinha build completo (verify dispensado)")
    return (f"fila {m['fila']} · run {m['run']}: o supervisor morreu no meio "
            f"do run ({m['como']}) e o registro ficou sem `run_end`{item}. "
            f"A branch da noite `{m['branch']}` está como ele deixou"
            + offer + f". Para rodar o build e deixar o run pronto para "
            f"aterrissar: {m['fechar']} (sem --yes só mostra o plano)")


def cmd_pending(argv):
    """`cepa-until pendentes [--repo R] [--json]`: what `/common:next` and
    `/common:doctor` read to say that a run is waiting for the owner (C6)."""
    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa until pendentes",
        summary=_sub_summary("pendentes"),
        description=(
            "A run is waiting for the owner when its branch is ready to land or it\n"
            "left items that only the owner can unblock (\"Fica com você\"). A run\n"
            "is dead when its supervisor died before writing the end of the run.\n"
            "Each line says which command takes the run forward.\n"
            "\n"
            "This is what /common:next and /common:doctor read to say that a run is\n"
            "waiting for you."),
        examples=[
            ("cepa until pendentes", "what is waiting for you, one line per run"),
            ("cepa until pendentes --json", "the same, as JSON for code"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "list printed (even empty)"),
            (2, "invalid usage"),
        ],
        see_also=["cepa until decide: answers what a run left for you",
                  "cepa until aterrissar: lands a waiting run",
                  "cepa until fecha-morto: closes a dead run"])
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=".", metavar="DIR",
                    help="repository root (default: the current directory)")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="prints JSON, for code")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    found = waiting_runs(Path(a.repo).resolve())
    dead = dead_runs(Path(a.repo).resolve())
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps({"runs": found, "mortos": dead},
                         ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    for m in dead:
        print(dead_run_phrase(m))
    for r in found:
        print(f"fila {r['fila']} · run {r['run']}: `{r['branch']}` espera "
              f"aterrissagem em `{r['destino']}`"
              + (f" ({r['fica_com_voce']} item(ns) em \"Fica com você\")"
                 if r["fica_com_voce"] else "")
              + f" — {r['comando']}")
    return 0


def has_upstream(repo):
    code, _ = git(["rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "@{u}"], repo)
    return code == 0


def main(argv=None):
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    if argv and argv[0] == "aterrissar":
        return cmd_land(argv[1:])
    if argv and argv[0] == "pendentes":
        return cmd_pending(argv[1:])
    if argv and argv[0] == "fecha-morto":
        return cmd_close_dead(argv[1:])
    if argv and argv[0] in ("decide", "decidir"):
        return cmd_decide(argv[1:])
    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa until",
        usage="cepa until <queue> (--for DURATION | --until HH:MM) [options]\n"
              "       cepa until <subcommand> ...",
        description=(
            "One item per subprocess: each item starts a fresh `claude -p`\n"
            "(/common:drain-plan <queue> --max 1), with a clean context, inside the\n"
            "until/<run> worktree the supervisor opens at the start. Running out of\n"
            "context stops being a failure and becomes the normal end of a subprocess.\n"
            "Reserving the item, recording the outcome and knowing the topology is\n"
            "the job of drain-plan + cepa plan. This command is the wiring around\n"
            "them: clock, circuit breaker, account quota, full build after each `done`\n"
            "item (red = the item becomes `blocked` and the branch rolls back) and log.\n"
            "\n"
            "The cut happens between items, never in the middle of one. Nothing goes to\n"
            "main or origin: afterwards, `cepa until decide <queue>/<run>` asks what\n"
            "was left for you, and `cepa until aterrissar` brings the branch into the\n"
            "clone."),
        commands=SUBCOMMANDS,
        examples=[
            ("cepa until wego --for 12h", "run the wego queue for 12 hours"),
            ("cepa until wego --until 07:00 --dry-run", "the run plan, nothing executed"),
            ("cepa until wego --for 8h --no-verify", "a repo without a build"),
            ("cepa until pendentes", "runs waiting for you"),
            ("cepa until decide wego/2026-11-03-2210", "answer what a run left for you"),
            ("cepa until aterrissar wego/2026-11-03-2210 --yes", "land the run branch"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "the run ended (deadline, empty queue, circuit breaker or quota), "
                "or --dry-run / nothing to do"),
            (2, "invalid usage (also with no arguments), or a refused start: "
                "`claude` missing, queue not executable, another live run of the "
                "queue, dirty tree, unknown build, run branch not created"),
            (130, "interrupted (Ctrl-C); the item in flight returns as an orphan "
                  "reservation"),
        ],
        see_also=["cepa prove: the same supervisor for the Jira Review column",
                  "cepa until-digest: the summary of a finished run",
                  "/common:until-review: what the owner has to do from a run",
                  "cepa plan: the queue this command runs"])
    ap.add_argument("queue", metavar="QUEUE",
                    help="queue name, as in .claude/queues/<name>/queue.yaml")
    window = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    window.add_argument("--for", dest="duration", metavar="DURATION",
                        help="how long to run (e.g. 12h, 90m)")
    window.add_argument("--until", dest="until_at", metavar="HH:MM",
                        help="what time to stop (the next HH:MM)")
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=".", metavar="DIR",
                    help="repository root (default: the current directory)")
    ap.add_argument("--max-failures", "--max-falhas", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MAX_FAILURES,
                    dest="max_failures", metavar="N",
                    help=f"circuit breaker: CONSECUTIVE failures that end the run "
                         f"(default {DEFAULT_MAX_FAILURES})")
    ap.add_argument("--max-blocked", "--max-travados", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MAX_BLOCKED,
                    dest="max_blocked", metavar="N",
                    help=f"CONSECUTIVE `blocked` items that end the run: the queue "
                         f"is stuck on an outside cause, and going on only "
                         f"rediscovers that cause (default {DEFAULT_MAX_BLOCKED})")
    ap.add_argument("--attempts-per-item", "--tentativas-por-item", type=int,
                    default=DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS_PER_ITEM, dest="attempts_per_item", metavar="N",
                    help=f"how many subprocesses one window spends on the same "
                         f"item before marking it `blocked` and moving to the "
                         f"next (default {DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS_PER_ITEM})")
    ap.add_argument("--min-reserve", "--reserva-minima", default=DEFAULT_MIN_RESERVE,
                    dest="min_reserve", metavar="DURATION",
                    help=f"does not start an item if less than this is left "
                         f"(default {DEFAULT_MIN_RESERVE})")
    ap.add_argument("--slack", "--folga", dest="slack", metavar="DURATION", default=DEFAULT_SLACK,
                    help=f"how far a running item may go past the deadline before "
                         f"it is killed (default {DEFAULT_SLACK})")
    ap.add_argument("--with-permissions", "--com-permissoes", action="store_true", dest="with_permissions",
                    help="does NOT pass --dangerously-skip-permissions. The "
                         "subprocess will hang on the first permission "
                         "request. Use only with someone watching")
    ap.add_argument("--dirty-ok", "--sujo-ok", action="store_true", dest="dirty_ok",
                    help="starts even with a dirty tree (refused by default: "
                         "otherwise what the run did cannot be told apart from "
                         "what was already there)")
    ap.add_argument("--verify", metavar="CMD",
                    help="the full build to run on the run branch after "
                         "each `done` item (default: from the root mvnw/gradlew, "
                         "or from the package.json scripts)")
    ap.add_argument("--no-verify", "--sem-verify", action="store_true", dest="no_verify",
                    help="skips the full build after items. Only for a "
                         "repo without a build")
    ap.add_argument("--no-analysis", "--sem-analise", action="store_true", dest="no_analysis",
                    help="skips /common:until-review at the end of the run")
    ap.add_argument("--full-title", "--titulo-inteiro", action="store_true", dest="full_title",
                    help="does not cut the item title at the terminal "
                         "width (the `.jsonl` always keeps the full title)")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", dest="dry",
                    help="shows the run plan and exits without executing anything")
    if not argv:
        ap.print_help(sys.stderr)
        return 2
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)

    repo = Path(a.repo).resolve()
    now = datetime.now()

    try:
        deadline = (now + parse_duration(a.duration)) if a.duration \
            else parse_until(a.until_at, now)
        reserve = parse_duration(a.min_reserve, "--min-reserve")
        slack = parse_duration(a.slack, "--slack")
    except ValueError as e:
        print(f"cepa-until: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    if a.max_failures < 1:
        print("cepa-until: --max-failures precisa ser >= 1", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if a.max_blocked < 1:
        print("cepa-until: --max-blocked precisa ser >= 1", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if a.attempts_per_item < 1:
        print("cepa-until: --attempts-per-item precisa ser >= 1 — com 0 o run "
              "marcaria `blocked` todo item antes de tentar", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if not shutil.which("claude"):
        print("cepa-until: `claude` não está no PATH — sem ele não há o que "
              "supervisionar", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    data, error = query_queue(a.queue, repo)
    if error:
        print(f"cepa-until: a fila {a.queue!r} não está executável — {error}",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    # Before the dirt guard, and with no `--dirty-ok` in the message nor as an
    # escape: two supervisors on the same queue is the failure. On 2026-10-15 19:08 the
    # refusal came out as "dirty tree" (the `plan.yaml` that the live run was writing) and
    # suggested the wrong escape (fb-20261015-4).
    alive = live_run_of_queue(repo, a.queue)
    if alive:
        try:
            end = datetime.fromisoformat(str(alive["prazo"])) \
                .strftime("%d/%m %H:%M")
        except ValueError:
            end = "?"
        print(f"cepa-until: já há um run desta fila em andamento "
              f"(run {alive['run']}, pid {alive['pid']}, prazo {end}). "
              "Espere ele terminar, ou encerre-o (kill do pid) antes de "
              "largar outro.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    dirt = dirty_tree(repo, live_run_ok=True)
    ghosts = ghost_deletions(repo, a.queue) if dirt else []
    if ghosts and not a.dirty_ok:
        # No `--dirty-ok` in the message on purpose: with it the next item runs
        # without the folder, and a broad commit turns the ghost deletion into a real
        # deletion.
        print(f"cepa-until: {len(ghosts)} arquivo(s) commitado(s) sumiram "
              "do disco fora do run: nenhum item do último run os tocou. "
              "Provável sincronização (Insync, Google Drive) apagando pasta "
              "do clone. Restaure e rode de novo:", file=sys.stderr)
        print(f"    git restore -- {' '.join(restore_targets(repo, ghosts))}",
              file=sys.stderr)
        for l in ghosts[:10]:
            print(f"     D {l}", file=sys.stderr)
        # The ` D` lines of porcelain come escaped; the deletions that are not
        # ghosts come back by the raw name.
        rest = [l for l in dirt if not l.startswith(" D ")] + \
            [f" D {f}" for f in vanished_from_disk(repo) if f not in ghosts]
        if rest:
            print(f"  E há mais {len(rest)} arquivo(s) modificado(s), que "
                  "precisam ser commitados ou limpos:", file=sys.stderr)
            for l in rest[:10]:
                print(f"    {l}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if dirt and not a.dirty_ok:
        print(f"cepa-until: a árvore tem {len(dirt)} arquivo(s) modificado(s). "
              "Commite ou limpe antes — de manhã não dá para separar o que o run "
              "fez do que já estava aqui. (--dirty-ok ignora este guarda.)",
              file=sys.stderr)
        for l in dirt[:10]:
            print(f"    {l}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    verify, verify_origin = verify_command(repo, a.verify, a.no_verify)
    if verify == "":
        print("cepa-until: não sei o build completo deste repo (não há `mvnw` "
              "nem `gradlew` na raiz, nem `tests/run-all.sh`, nem `package.json` com "
              "script `build` ou `test`). Passe `--verify '<comando>'`, ou "
              "`--no-verify` se o repo não tem build — sem isso um card pode "
              "fechar `done` com o build vermelho e o próximo começar em cima "
              "dele.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    ledger_dir = qp.queue_dir(repo, a.queue) / "until"
    ledger_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    run_id = now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d-%H%M")
    ledger = ledger_dir / f"{run_id}.jsonl"
    log = ledger_dir / f"{run_id}.log"

    # Short header (A6): the 09/26 run opened with 15 configuration lines
    # and absolute paths through the Insync folder taking up half a screen.
    nxt = (data.get("batch") or [{}])[0]
    t = data.get("totals") or {}
    SCREEN.full_title = a.full_title
    lbl = lambda r: SCREEN.c("cinza", r)  # noqa: E731
    print(SCREEN.c("negrito", "cepa-until") + " · fila "
          + SCREEN.c("ciano", str(qp.queue_name_of(data))) + f" · {repo.name} · até "
          + SCREEN.c("negrito", deadline.strftime('%d/%m %H:%M'))
          + f" ({human(deadline - now)})")
    if SCREEN.enabled:
        print(lbl("  janela : ") + f"{now.strftime('%H:%M')} → "
              f"{deadline.strftime('%H:%M')}  " + SCREEN.bar(0.0, 24))
    print(lbl("  noite  : ") + "trabalha em " + SCREEN.c("ciano", f"`until/{run_id}`")
          + ", numa worktree fora do clone; "
          + SCREEN.c("ciano", f"`{current_branch(repo)}`") + " e o origin não mudam")
    print(lbl("  build  : ") + (SCREEN.c("ciano", verify) + " depois de cada item "
                                f"done ({verify_origin})" if verify else
                                f"dispensado ({verify_origin})"))
    print(lbl("  paradas: ") + f"{a.max_failures} itens seguidos sem avançar (disjuntor) · "
          f"{a.max_blocked} itens `blocked` seguidos (fila travada) · "
          f"{a.attempts_per_item} tentativa(s) por item")
    print(lbl("  tempo  : ") + f"não começa item com menos de {human(reserve)}; mata "
          f"item que passar {human(slack)} do prazo")
    print(lbl("  permissões: ")
          + SCREEN.c("amarelo", "PEDE (vai travar sem alguém olhando)" if a.with_permissions
                   else "--dangerously-skip-permissions LIGADO"))
    print(lbl("  1º item: ")
          + SCREEN.c("negrito", nxt.get('id', '(nenhum — fila sem item executável)'))
          + (SCREEN.c("cinza", SCREEN.truncate(f" — {nxt.get('title')}", slack=40))
             if nxt.get("id") else "")
          + f" · fila: {t.get('por_status', {}).get('pending', 0)} "
            f"pendente(s), {t.get('por_status', {}).get('done', 0)} done")
    inheritance = inheritance_from_previous_run(repo, a.queue, data.get("path"))
    for h in inheritance:
        print(lbl("  herda  : ") + f"`{h['branch']}` ({h['commits']} commit(s) que o "
              f"clone não tem) — {', '.join(h['itens'])} ficou pela metade "
              "lá, e a branch da noite nasce com esses commits")

    if a.dry:
        print("\n(--dry-run: nada foi executado)")
        return 0
    if not data.get("batch"):
        stop = data.get("stop") or {}
        print(f"\nnada a fazer: {stop.get('reason')} — {stop.get('detail')}")
        return 0

    # A closed terminal tab sends SIGHUP to the terminal's group. `claude`
    # runs in its own session and survives; the supervisor used to die silently in the middle
    # of the item, with no `verify`, `item_end` or `run_end` (WEGO 2026-09-28-2003).
    # From here on it ignores SIGHUP and writes to the screen without depending on it.
    signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIG_IGN)
    sys.stdout = TolerantOutput(sys.stdout)
    sys.stderr = TolerantOutput(sys.stderr)
    pid, host = os.getpid(), socket.gethostname()

    def log_event(event):
        event["quando"] = datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
        with ledger.open("a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")

    # The clone's HEAD BEFORE the inheritance merge: it is up to here that the
    # red of an inherited item goes back, whose commits from the previous run enter through the
    # merge and didn't go through this run's build.
    clone_base = head_of(repo)
    tree, start_branch, error = open_run_branch(repo, run_id, inheritance)
    if error:
        print(f"cepa-until: não consegui criar a branch da noite "
              f"`{start_branch}`: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    # With inheritance, the base is HEAD AFTER the merge: what the night counts as
    # "commits over the launch" is what it did, not what it inherited.
    run_base = head_of(tree)
    log_event({"evento": "run_start", "fila": a.queue, "prazo": deadline.isoformat(),
              "max_falhas": a.max_failures, "max_travados": a.max_blocked,
              "branch": start_branch,
              "arvore": str(tree), "base": run_base,
              "herdou": inheritance,
              "branch_do_clone": current_branch(repo), "verify": verify,
              "pid": pid, "host": host})
    # The run state, next to the `.jsonl` (C6): `rodando` now, and at the end
    # `esperando-dono` (there is an action or pending item) or `encerrado`. It is written BEFORE
    # the model analysis, which may fail on the quota (C7); `/common:until-review`
    # comments on the same list, and `/common:next` and `/common:doctor` read it.
    state_path = ledger.parent / (ledger.stem + ".estado.json")

    def save_state(run_state, **rest):
        body = {"run": run_id, "fila": a.queue, "estado": run_state,
                 "branch": start_branch, "registro": ledger.name,
                 "verify": verify, "pid": pid, "host": host,
                 "arvore": str(tree), "prazo": deadline.isoformat(),
                 "atualizado": datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")}
        body.update(rest)
        tmp = state_path.parent / (state_path.name + ".tmp")
        try:
            tmp.write_text(json.dumps(body, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)
                           + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
            os.replace(tmp, state_path)
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"  aviso: não gravei o estado do run em {state_path}: "
                  f"{e}")

    save_state("rodando")

    # What is in flight when a SIGTERM or Ctrl+C arrives: the item, the phase
    # (`item` is `claude`, `verify` is the full build) and the child's pid, which
    # runs in its own session and doesn't receive the signal.
    in_flight = {}
    closed = [False]

    def interrupt(signum, _frame):
        name = signal.Signals(signum).name
        if closed[0]:
            raise SystemExit(128 + signum)
        closed[0] = True
        flight = dict(in_flight) or None
        child = (flight or {}).get("pid_filho")
        # The child runs in its own session and would go on by itself: a card changing
        # with nobody to run the full build afterwards. Dead, its reservation
        # becomes orphan and the next `queue` returns the item.
        terminated = (terminate_group(child, min(SIGTERM_GRACE, 10))
                     if child else None)
        log_event({"evento": "run_interrompido", "sinal": name,
                  "id": (flight or {}).get("id"), "fase": (flight or {}).get("fase"),
                  "pid_filho": child, "filho_encerrado": terminated})
        save_state("interrompido", sinal=name, item_em_voo=flight)
        print(f"\ncepa-until: interrompido por {name}"
              + (f" com {flight['id']} em voo ({flight.get('fase')})" if flight else
                 " entre itens")
              + f". Registrei em {short_path(ledger, repo)}.", file=sys.stderr)
        if child:
            print(f"  o processo filho (pid {child}) "
                  + ("foi encerrado; o próximo `queue` devolve o item como "
                     "reserva órfã." if terminated else
                     "NÃO morreu, e segue sem supervisor."), file=sys.stderr)
        print(f"  para rodar o build que faltou e deixar o run pronto para "
              f"aterrissar: cepa-until fecha-morto {a.queue}/{run_id}",
              file=sys.stderr)
        raise SystemExit(128 + signum)

    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, interrupt)
    signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, interrupt)

    def launched(child_pid):
        in_flight["pid_filho"] = child_pid
    kept_side_branches = []
    for side, patch, side_error in clean_side_branches(
            repo, data.get("path"), ledger_dir / f"{run_id}.laterais",
            start_branch):
        if patch:
            log_event({"evento": "lateral_apagada", "branch": side,
                      "patch": patch})
            print(f"  lateral     : apaguei `{side}` (item fechado); cópia em "
                  f"{Path(patch).relative_to(repo)}")
        else:
            log_event({"evento": "lateral_mantida", "branch": side,
                      "erro": side_error})
            kept_side_branches.append((side, side_error))
            print(f"  lateral     : mantive `{side}`: não gravei a cópia "
                  f"({side_error})")
    # What the night DELIVERED (done with a green build on the night branch) and what
    # stalled (`blocked`). Both count as progress for the circuit breaker —
    # taking an item out of the queue with a reason is not a run failure —, but the summary
    # can't add them up: on 09/23 "25 with progress" hid 20 stalled.
    delivered, blocked_items, reds, without_commit = [], [], [], []

    consecutive_failures = 0
    # The `blocked` of the current sequence. Only an outcome that is not `blocked`
    # (done, dropped, human route) resets it; an attempt with no progress belongs to the breaker
    # and doesn't touch this.
    consecutive_blocked = []
    done_items, failed, items = [], [], 0
    # How many times THIS window has already launched a subprocess for each item, and
    # what it took out of the way through exhaustion or the account usage ceiling.
    attempts, exhausted, limited = {}, [], []
    # The HEAD at the start of each item's 1st attempt in this window, and how many
    # items had already been delivered by then: it is up to that HEAD that the red returns
    # the night branch, and only if nobody closed `done` in the middle (C4).
    first = {}
    # Inherited item (left half-done in the previous run): its 1st attempt
    # started there, and the return point is the clone before the inheritance merge. The
    # other inherited items still open enter the "in the middle": the return would take
    # their work out too, and then the supervisor stops instead of resetting (C4).
    inherited = {str(i) for h in inheritance for i in h.get("itens") or []}
    for i in inherited:
        first[i] = (clone_base, 0)

    def in_the_middle_of(ident, n_before):
        others = []
        if ident in inherited:
            others = [f"{o} (herdado do run anterior, ainda aberto)"
                      for o in sorted(inherited - {ident})
                      if o not in delivered]
        return delivered[n_before:] + others

    # The outcome of each item in this window, in the order it appeared: it is the
    # "one line per item" list at the end (A4). The item's last outcome wins.
    outcomes = {}
    # The `total_cost_usd` of each `claude` round: the cost only showed up in the
    # model analysis (A6), and the analysis may not run.
    # One cost per session (`round_costs`), not per `result` block.
    costs = {}

    def outcome(ident, kind, text):
        outcomes[ident] = (kind, text)

    end_reason, end_detail = None, None
    # The 5h quota seen through the `rate_limit_event`s: the start reading of each
    # attempt (it is where an item's cost comes from), the last reading, whether it
    # already includes the previous item, and the waits done.
    starts, last_reading, fresh_reading = [], None, False
    waits, consecutive_waits = [], 0
    # The network drops: [item, when it dropped, when it came back or None], and the
    # consecutive ones.
    drops, consecutive_drops = [], 0
    # Items started with a tight quota and the reset outside the window.
    tight = []
    # Plugin hooks that the night branch changed and that the screen has already warned about. The
    # base is the clone's HEAD, and not the night's, so the inheritance counts: what
    # it brought is not in the installed plugin either.
    notified_hooks = []

    def notify_hooks(origin):
        new_items = [f for f in changed_hooks(tree, clone_base)
                 if f not in notified_hooks]
        if not new_items:
            return
        notified_hooks.extend(new_items)
        log_event({"evento": "hook_so_apos_reinstalar", "id": origin,
                  "arquivos": new_items})
        step(f"{origin} mudou hook de plugin "
              f"({', '.join(new_items)}): só passa a valer depois de aterrissar "
              "a branch da noite e rodar `bin/install.sh`. Até lá as "
              "rodadas desta noite seguem com a versão instalada")

    print()
    while True:
        in_flight.clear()
        notify_hooks(ident if items else "a herança da largada")
        remaining = deadline - datetime.now()
        if remaining < reserve:
            end_reason = "prazo"
            end_detail = (f"sobram {human(remaining)}, menos que a reserva "
                           f"mínima de {human(reserve)} — começar um item "
                           "agora seria trabalho jogado fora")
            break

        branch_now, git_error = read_branch(tree)
        if git_error:
            # A git that doesn't respond is not a branch switch. Tries to rebuild the
            # worktree link; if the branch goes back to the launch one, the
            # night goes on.
            repair_failure = repair_link(repo, tree, start_branch)
            if not repair_failure:
                branch_now, after = read_branch(tree)
                if after:
                    repair_failure = f"reparei, e o git ainda diz: {after}"
            log_event({"evento": "git_reparo", "erro": git_error,
                      "reparou": not repair_failure, "falha": repair_failure})
            if repair_failure:
                end_reason = "git-quebrado"
                end_detail = (
                    f"o git parou de responder na worktree da noite `{tree}`"
                    f" ({git_error}) e o reparo não voltou: {repair_failure}. "
                    "Ninguém trocou de branch; o que está no disco da worktree "
                    "continua lá")
                break
            print(SCREEN.stamp() + f" o git não respondia "
                  f"na worktree da noite ({git_error}); refiz a ligação dela "
                  "com o clone e sigo")
        if branch_now != start_branch:
            end_reason = "branch-mudou"
            end_detail = (
                f"a largada foi em `{start_branch}` e agora estamos em "
                f"`{branch_now}` — alguém trocou de branch no meio do run. "
                "Seguir espalharia os commits da noite por branches que "
                "ninguém vai buscar de manhã, que é exatamente o que a decisão "
                "de commitar por item numa branch só existe para impedir")
            break

        data, error = query_queue(a.queue, repo)
        if error:
            end_reason, end_detail = "fila-ilegivel", error
            break
        for warning in data.get("warnings") or []:
            print(f"  aviso: {warning}")
            log_event({"evento": "aviso", "texto": warning})
        if not data.get("batch"):
            stop = data.get("stop") or {}
            end_reason = stop.get("reason") or "fim-da-fila"
            end_detail = stop.get("detail") or "a fila não tem item executável"
            break

        item = data["batch"][0]
        ident = item["id"]
        plan_path = data.get("path")

        # Doesn't start an item the 5h quota can't hold: cut in the middle, it
        # wastes what it already spent and leaves the tree half-done.
        reset = quota_pause(last_reading, fresh_reading,
                              item_cost(starts), datetime.now())
        if reset:
            wake_at = reset + timedelta(seconds=RESET_MARGIN)
            usage = last_reading[0]
            if deadline - wake_at < reserve:
                # The reset doesn't fit in the window. Waiting would mean stopping for good; the
                # cut in the middle is recoverable (worktree + orphan reservation). Starts
                # and warns — half an item is worth more than a stalled window.
                print(SCREEN.stamp() + f" cota de 5h em "
                      f"{usage:.0%} e o próximo item talvez não caiba; o reset "
                      f"({reset.strftime('%H:%M')}) não cabe na janela (fecha "
                      f"às {deadline.strftime('%H:%M')}) · começo assim mesmo — "
                      "se cortar, o próximo run retoma da worktree")
                log_event({"evento": "cota_apertada", "uso": usage,
                          "custo_item": item_cost(starts),
                          "reset": reset.isoformat(), "id": ident})
                tight.append((ident, usage, reset))
            else:
                print(SCREEN.stamp() + f" cota de 5h em "
                      f"{usage:.0%}, o próximo item não cabe · espero o reset e "
                      f"retomo às {wake_at.strftime('%H:%M')}")
                log_event({"evento": "pausa_de_cota", "uso": usage,
                          "custo_item": item_cost(starts),
                          "reset": reset.isoformat(),
                          "acorda": wake_at.isoformat()})
                waits.append(("antes do item", ident, reset))
                wait_until(wake_at)
                last_reading, fresh_reading = None, False
                continue

        items += 1
        attempts[ident] = attempts.get(ident, 0) + 1
        round_n = attempts[ident]

        if SCREEN.enabled:
            # Block per item: time, id, attempt no., how much of the window
            # is gone, and the title cut to the width (whole in the `.jsonl`).
            if items > 1:
                print()
            window_total = max((deadline - now).total_seconds(), 1)
            print(SCREEN.stamp() + " " + SCREEN.c("negrito", ident)
                  + (SCREEN.c("amarelo", f" tentativa {round_n}/{a.attempts_per_item}")
                     if round_n > 1 else "")
                  + SCREEN.c("cinza", f"   item {items}   ")
                  + SCREEN.bar(1 - remaining.total_seconds() / window_total)
                  + SCREEN.c("cinza", f" {human(remaining)} restam"))
            print(SCREEN.c("cinza", "       " + SCREEN.truncate(str(item.get('title')), slack=8)))
        else:
            print(f"[{datetime.now().strftime('%H:%M')}] {ident} — {item.get('title')} "
                  f"({human(remaining)} restantes"
                  + (f", tentativa {round_n}/{a.attempts_per_item}" if round_n > 1 else "") + ")")
        before = head_of(tree)
        first.setdefault(ident, (before, len(delivered)))
        log_event({"evento": "item_start", "id": ident, "title": item.get("title"),
                  "restante_seg": int(remaining.total_seconds()),
                  "tentativa": round_n, "twg_version": installed_twg_version(),
                  "head": before})

        in_flight.update(id=ident, fase="item", tentativa=round_n)
        limit = (remaining + slack).total_seconds()
        code, killed, spent, output = run_item(
            a.queue, tree, start_branch, a.with_permissions, limit, log,
            on_launch=launched)
        in_flight.pop("pid_filho", None)

        # Uncommitted leftovers don't carry over to the next item.
        if dirty_tree(tree):
            sha, leftover_error = stash_leftover(tree, run_id, ident)
            log_event({"evento": "sobra_guardada", "id": ident, "stash": sha,
                      "erro": leftover_error})
            step(f"o item deixou arquivos sem commit"
                  + (f"; guardei no stash {sha[:10]}" if sha else
                     f" e NÃO consegui guardá-los: {leftover_error}"))

        head_after = head_of(tree)
        n_commits = 0
        if before and head_after and before != head_after:
            c, count = git(["rev-list", "--count", f"{before}..{head_after}"],
                              tree)
            n_commits = int(count) if c == 0 and count.isdigit() else -1

        # A commit on the night branch is progress, with or without an outcome:
        # WEGO-2283 was killed by the slack with 15 commits and came out `progresso: false`,
        # and the circuit breaker and the attempt ceiling would treat it as stalled. The
        # next attempt (or the next run, through inheritance) starts from there.
        after, item_error = read_item(plan_path, ident)
        if item_error:
            run_state = "?"
            pending_item = None
            progress = n_commits > 0
        else:
            run_state = str(after.get("status") or "pending").strip().lower()
            pending_item = after.get("human_pending")
            progress = (run_state in TERMINAL_STATES or pending_item is not None
                         or n_commits > 0)

        readings = quota_readings(output)
        round_costs(costs, output)
        if readings:
            starts.append(readings[0])
            last_reading = readings[-1]
            fresh_reading = readings[-1][0] > readings[0][0]

        log_event({"evento": "item_end", "id": ident, "status": run_state,
                  "human_pending": pending_item, "exit_code": code,
                  "timeout": killed, "segundos": int(spent),
                  "tentativa": round_n, "progresso": progress,
                  "commits": n_commits,
                  "cota_5h": ([readings[0][0], readings[-1][0]]
                              if readings else None)})

        back_now = False
        unstable = False
        # The full build of the night branch, after each `done` that
        # committed. The supervisor runs it, not the agent: the agent may
        # run it before the last refactor, run it in two halves or skip the
        # validation phase (all three happened on 09/23).
        if run_state == "done" and n_commits == 0:
            without_commit.append(ident)
            log_event({"evento": "done_sem_commit", "id": ident})
            step("`done` sem nenhum commit na branch da noite: o "
                  "trabalho, se houve, foi parar em outra branch")
        elif run_state == "done" and verify:
            step(f"build completo: {verify}")
            left = (deadline + slack - datetime.now()).total_seconds()
            in_flight["fase"] = "verify"
            green, verify_sec, verify_reason = run_verify(
                verify, tree, left, log, on_launch=launched)
            in_flight.pop("pid_filho", None)
            log_event({"evento": "verify", "id": ident, "verde": green,
                      "segundos": int(verify_sec), "motivo": verify_reason})
            if not green:
                # Second full build on the same code (Revision 3, exception
                # taken to rule 4 of green-or-revert, requested by the owner on
                # 09/26). With no time for it, it is a red return: the next
                # attempt does the rest.
                left = (deadline + slack - datetime.now()).total_seconds()
                if left >= verify_sec:
                    step(f"vermelho ({verify_reason}); rodo o "
                          "build completo de novo, no mesmo código")
                    green, sec2, reason2 = run_verify(verify, tree, left,
                                                       log, on_launch=launched)
                    in_flight.pop("pid_filho", None)
                    log_event({"evento": "verify", "id": ident, "verde": green,
                              "segundos": int(sec2), "motivo": reason2,
                              "repeticao": 2})
                else:
                    reason2 = "não coube no que sobra da janela"
                if green:
                    log_event({"evento": "verify_repetido_verde", "id": ident,
                              "motivo_1": verify_reason})
                    emit_telemetry("build_instavel", repo, card=ident,
                                     run=run_id, fila=a.queue,
                                     motivo=verify_reason)
                    step("verde na 2ª vez: build instável, "
                          "registrado na telemetria")
                    unstable = True
            if green:
                step(f"verde ({human(timedelta(seconds=verify_sec))})")
            else:
                back = red_returns(ledger_dir, ident) + 1
                since, n_before = first[ident]
                side_branch, undo_error = undo_item(
                    repo, tree, run_id, ident, since,
                    in_the_middle=in_the_middle_of(ident, n_before), back=back)
                last = back >= MAX_RED_RETURNS or bool(undo_error)
                new_status = "blocked" if last else "pending"
                if side_branch:
                    # The reset already took the attempts away; the next one starts from zero.
                    first.pop(ident, None)
                    inherited.discard(ident)
                    evid = (f"Esta é a volta {back} de "
                            f"{MAX_RED_RETURNS}: o item fechou `done`, "
                            f"mas o build completo da branch da noite "
                            f"(`{verify}`) {verify_reason}, e o 2º build "
                            f"{reason2 or 'também ficou vermelho'}. Saída no "
                            f"`.log` do run {run_id}. Os commits de todas as "
                            f"tentativas estão em `{side_branch}` e a branch da "
                            f"noite voltou para {since[:10]}. ")
                    if last:
                        evid += ("Marquei `blocked`: o item já voltou com o "
                                 "recado e ficou vermelho de novo. O card no "
                                 "Jira pode ter ido para Review antes do "
                                 "build — confira.")
                    else:
                        evid += ("O item voltou para `pending`: aproveite a "
                                 "lateral (`git cherry-pick` ou `git merge` "
                                 "dentro da tentativa) ou refaça; o build do "
                                 "supervisor julga o resultado. Desabilitar ou "
                                 "apagar o teste que falhou não conta como "
                                 "conserto.")
                else:
                    evid = (f"O item fechou `done`, mas o build completo da "
                            f"branch da noite (`{verify}`) {verify_reason}. "
                            f"Saída no `.log` do run {run_id}. NÃO consegui "
                            f"tirar os commits da branch da noite: "
                            f"{undo_error}")
                finish_error = finish_item(
                    a.queue, repo, ident, new_status, evid,
                    "o agente entregou, mas a bateria completa de testes do "
                    "projeto falhou depois dele, e falhou de novo quando o "
                    "item voltou para ser corrigido." if new_status == "blocked"
                    else None)
                reds.append((ident, side_branch, verify_reason))
                log_event({"evento": "verify_vermelho", "id": ident,
                          "lateral": side_branch, "erro": undo_error or finish_error})
                if side_branch:
                    log_event({"evento": "volta_vermelha", "id": ident,
                              "volta": back, "lateral": side_branch,
                              "motivo": verify_reason, "motivo_2": reason2,
                              "status": new_status})
                    back_now = True
                step(f"VERMELHO ({verify_reason}): commits "
                      f"guardados em `{side_branch}`, item marcado `{new_status}`"
                      + (f" (volta {back}/{MAX_RED_RETURNS})"
                         if side_branch else ""))
                run_state = new_status
                if undo_error:
                    outcome(ident, "travado",
                             f"build vermelho ({verify_reason}) e os commits "
                             f"continuam na branch da noite: {undo_error}")
                    end_reason = "verify-vermelho"
                    end_detail = (f"o build ficou vermelho depois do {ident} e "
                                   f"não consegui desfazer os commits dele "
                                   f"({undo_error}); o próximo card começaria "
                                   "em cima de código quebrado")
                    break
        # The build only runs after `done`: an item that the agent closes
        # `blocked` after committing left those commits on the night
        # branch with no build, underneath the next card. They go to the side branch, like
        # those of the exhausted item, and the evidence says where they are.
        elif run_state == "blocked" and ident in first:
            since, n_before = first[ident]
            if since and head_of(tree) != since:
                side_branch, undo_error = undo_item(
                    repo, tree, run_id, ident, since,
                    in_the_middle=in_the_middle_of(ident, n_before), suffix="travado")
                finish_error = None
                if side_branch:
                    first.pop(ident, None)
                    inherited.discard(ident)
                    reread, _ = read_item(plan_path, ident)
                    ev = str((reread or {}).get("evidence") or "").strip()
                    # The agent's human section survives the re-finish: only
                    # the agents' section gets the supervisor's note.
                    kept = (reread or {}).get("owner_summary") or {}
                    finish_error = finish_item(
                        a.queue, repo, ident, "blocked",
                        (ev + " " if ev else "") +
                        f"[supervisor] Os commits do item, que não passaram "
                        f"pelo build do supervisor (ele só roda depois de "
                        f"`done`), estão em `{side_branch}`; a branch da noite "
                        f"voltou para {since[:10]}.",
                        None if isinstance(kept, dict) and kept.get("impede")
                        else "o agente marcou o item como travado sem explicar "
                             "o motivo em palavras simples.",
                        kept if isinstance(kept, dict) else None)
                log_event({"evento": "travado_separado", "id": ident,
                          "lateral": side_branch,
                          "erro": undo_error or finish_error})
                if undo_error:
                    outcome(ident, "travado",
                             "`blocked` com commits que continuam na branch "
                             f"da noite sem build: {undo_error}")
                    end_reason = "item-preso"
                    end_detail = (
                        f"{ident} saiu `blocked` com commits que não passaram "
                        f"pelo build, e não consegui tirá-los da branch da "
                        f"noite ({undo_error}); o próximo card começaria em "
                        "cima deles")
                    break
                step(f"`blocked` com commits: guardei em "
                      f"`{side_branch}` e a branch da noite voltou para "
                      f"{since[:10]}")
        if run_state == "done":
            delivered.append(ident)
        elif run_state == "blocked":
            # The reason goes along: the end-of-run summary is where the owner reads what to do,
            # and on 09/25 it only said "Travados (1)" while the command that
            # WEGO-2334 left for him to run was in the queue's `evidence`.
            reread, _ = read_item(plan_path, ident)
            reread = reread or {}
            blocked_items.append((ident, reread.get("human_pending"),
                             reread.get("evidence")))

        if back_now:
            outcome(ident, "volta-vermelha" if run_state == "pending" else
                     "travado",
                     f"volta vermelha {back}/{MAX_RED_RETURNS} "
                     f"({verify_reason}); commits em `{side_branch}`, "
                     + ("voltou para `pending` com o recado"
                        if run_state == "pending" else "marcado `blocked`"))
        elif pending_item:
            outcome(ident, "rota-humana",
                     f"`{run_state}`, espera por você: {pending_item}")
        elif run_state == "done" and ident in without_commit:
            outcome(ident, "done-sem-commit",
                     "`done` sem commit na branch da noite: procure o "
                     "trabalho em outra branch")
        elif run_state == "done":
            outcome(ident, "entregue",
                     "entregue" + ("; build verde na 2ª vez (instável)"
                                   if unstable else
                                   ", build verde" if verify else ""))
        elif run_state in ("blocked", "dropped"):
            reread, _ = read_item(plan_path, ident)
            ev = (reread or {}).get("evidence")
            outcome(ident, "travado" if run_state == "blocked" else "dropped",
                     f"`{run_state}`: "
                     + (summarize_reason(ev) if ev else
                        "o item não registrou motivo na fila"))
        elif n_commits > 0:
            outcome(ident, "em-andamento",
                     f"{n_commits} commit(s) sem fechar; a próxima tentativa "
                     "(ou o próximo run) parte daí")

        # The red return counts as a consecutive failure (Revision 3, 4e): a
        # broken environment makes every build red, and without this each card
        # would go back to `pending` with no counter seeing the problem. The
        # last return (`blocked`) also enters the stalled-queue counter.
        if back_now:
            consecutive_failures += 1
            if run_state == "blocked":
                consecutive_blocked.append(ident)
            if consecutive_failures >= a.max_failures:
                end_reason = "disjuntor"
                end_detail = (f"{consecutive_failures} itens seguidos sem fechar "
                               "verde (o último, volta vermelha do "
                               f"{ident}) — isso é sistêmico, não azar; "
                               "seguir queimaria a janela no mesmo problema")
                break
            if len(consecutive_blocked) >= a.max_blocked:
                end_reason = "fila-travada"
                end_detail = (
                    f"{len(consecutive_blocked)} itens seguidos saíram `blocked` "
                    f"({', '.join(consecutive_blocked)}); o motivo de cada um "
                    "está no `evidence` da fila")
                break
            continue

        # The NETWORK dropped, before the ceiling and the breaker: the item didn't move because
        # `claude` couldn't reach the API. Gives back the turn, waits for the network to return and
        # resumes the same item — the orphan reservation is claimed by `start`.
        if not progress and network_drop(output):
            attempts[ident] -= 1
            consecutive_drops += 1
            dropped_at = datetime.now()
            until_at = deadline - reserve
            fits = consecutive_drops < MAX_CONSECUTIVE_DROPS and until_at > dropped_at
            log_event({"evento": "queda_de_rede", "id": ident, "espera": fits,
                      "ate": until_at.isoformat(), "seguidas": consecutive_drops})
            # Counts at the moment it dropped, not when it returns: the drop that STOPS the
            # run is precisely the one that doesn't return, and counted only on return it
            # vanished from `run_end` (the 2026-09-26-2203 run ended `sem-rede`
            # with `quedas_de_rede: 0`). `voltou` stays None until the network is back.
            drop = [ident, dropped_at, None]
            drops.append(drop)
            outcome(ident, "sem-rede", "a rede caiu durante o item; não é "
                     "falha dele, e ele continua onde estava")
            step(f"SEM REDE: o `claude` não alcançou a API — não é "
                  "falha do item")
            if fits:
                step(f"sondo {NETWORK_PROBE} até a rede voltar (no "
                      f"máximo até {until_at.strftime('%H:%M')}) e retomo o {ident}")
                if wait_for_network(until_at):
                    returned = datetime.now()
                    drop[2] = returned
                    log_event({"evento": "rede_voltou", "id": ident,
                              "segundos": int((returned - dropped_at).total_seconds())})
                    print(SCREEN.stamp(returned) + f" rede de volta "
                          f"({human(returned - dropped_at)} sem)")
                    continue
                end_reason = "sem-rede"
                end_detail = (
                    f"a rede caiu durante o {ident} às {dropped_at.strftime('%H:%M')} "
                    f"e não voltou até {until_at.strftime('%H:%M')}, o último "
                    "instante em que ainda cabia começar um item na janela. O "
                    "item continua onde estava, sem culpa registrada")
                break
            end_reason = "sem-rede"
            if consecutive_drops >= MAX_CONSECUTIVE_DROPS:
                because = (f"é a {consecutive_drops}ª queda seguida sem progresso "
                          "entre elas — a sonda enxerga a rede, o `claude` não")
            else:
                because = "não sobra tempo na janela para esperar a rede voltar"
            end_detail = (
                f"o `claude` não alcançou a API durante o {ident} e não dá para "
                f"esperar: {because}. O item continua onde estava, sem culpa "
                "registrada")
            break

        # The ACCOUNT usage ceiling, before the circuit breaker. Without this separation the
        # message "You've hit your session limit" becomes "the item didn't move
        # from its place" and the morning report accuses the wrong card. It is only consulted
        # when the item didn't move — an attempt that CLOSED the item doesn't become
        # a stop, whatever happens afterwards in the output.
        if not progress:
            hit, reset, reset_at = usage_limit(output)
            if hit:
                limited.append((ident, reset))
                outcome(ident, "limite-de-uso", "interrompido pelo teto de "
                         "uso da conta; não é falha do item")
                # The attempt cut by the ceiling is not the item's: gives back the turn.
                attempts[ident] -= 1
                consecutive_waits += 1
                wake_at = (reset_at + timedelta(seconds=RESET_MARGIN)
                          if reset_at else None)
                fits = (wake_at is not None and wake_at > datetime.now()
                        and deadline - wake_at >= reserve
                        and consecutive_waits < MAX_CONSECUTIVE_WAITS)
                log_event({"evento": "limite_de_uso", "id": ident, "reset": reset,
                          "reset_em": reset_at.isoformat() if reset_at else None,
                          "espera": fits})
                step(f"LIMITE DE USO DA CONTA"
                      + (f" · reseta {reset}" if reset else "")
                      + " — não é falha do item")
                if fits:
                    step(f"espero o reset e retomo o {ident} às "
                          f"{wake_at.strftime('%H:%M')}")
                    waits.append(("item cortado", ident, reset_at))
                    wait_until(wake_at)
                    last_reading, fresh_reading = None, False
                    continue
                end_reason = "limite-de-uso"
                if consecutive_waits >= MAX_CONSECUTIVE_WAITS:
                    because = (f"é a {consecutive_waits}ª vez seguida sem progresso "
                              "entre elas — o reset anunciado não está levantando "
                              "o teto")
                elif reset_at is None:
                    because = "o `claude` não disse quando reseta"
                else:
                    because = (f"o reset ({reset_at.strftime('%H:%M')}) não deixa "
                              f"a reserva mínima antes do fim da janela "
                              f"({deadline.strftime('%H:%M')})")
                end_detail = (
                    f"a conta bateu o teto de uso da Claude durante o {ident} e "
                    f"não dá para esperar: {because}. O item continua onde "
                    "estava, sem culpa registrada")
                break

        if progress:
            consecutive_failures = 0
            consecutive_waits = 0
            consecutive_drops = 0
            done_items.append((ident, run_state, pending_item))
            mark = run_state
            if pending_item:
                mark += " · rota humana em aberto"
            if run_state not in TERMINAL_STATES and not pending_item:
                mark += f" · {n_commits} commit(s) sem fechar"
            step(f"{mark} ({human(timedelta(seconds=spent))})")

            if run_state == "blocked":
                consecutive_blocked.append(ident)
            else:
                consecutive_blocked = []
            if len(consecutive_blocked) >= a.max_blocked:
                end_reason = "fila-travada"
                end_detail = (
                    f"{len(consecutive_blocked)} itens seguidos saíram `blocked` "
                    f"({', '.join(consecutive_blocked)}) — a fila está travando "
                    "por uma condição de fora, não por falha dos itens. Seguir "
                    "redescobriria a mesma causa a cada item; o motivo de cada "
                    "um está no `evidence` da fila")
                break
        else:
            consecutive_failures += 1
            failed.append((ident, run_state, code, killed))
            reason_text = ("morto por timeout" if killed else
                     "não consegui nem lançar o `claude`" if code == -2 else
                     f"claude saiu {code}" if code else
                     "o item não saiu do lugar")
            outcome(ident, "sem-progresso",
                     f"sem progresso ({reason_text}), status `{run_state}`")
            step(f"SEM PROGRESSO: {reason_text} "
                  f"(status ainda `{run_state}`) · {consecutive_failures}/{a.max_failures}")

            if round_n >= a.attempts_per_item:
                # An earlier attempt may have committed without closing: those
                # commits never went through the build and can't stay underneath
                # the next card (C4).
                side_branch, undo_error = None, None
                since, n_before = first[ident]
                if since and head_of(tree) != since:
                    side_branch, undo_error = undo_item(
                        repo, tree, run_id, ident, since,
                        in_the_middle=in_the_middle_of(ident, n_before), suffix="parado")
                    log_event({"evento": "tentativas_separadas", "id": ident,
                              "lateral": side_branch, "erro": undo_error})
                    if side_branch:
                        first.pop(ident, None)
                        inherited.discard(ident)
                if undo_error:
                    end_reason = "item-preso"
                    end_detail = (
                        f"{ident} gastou as {round_n} tentativas com commits que "
                        f"não passaram pelo build, e não consegui tirá-los da "
                        f"branch da noite ({undo_error}); o próximo card "
                        "começaria em cima deles")
                    break
                block_error = block_item(a.queue, repo, ident, round_n, side_branch)
                if block_error:
                    end_reason = "item-preso"
                    end_detail = (
                        f"{ident} gastou as {round_n} tentativas e eu não consegui "
                        f"tirá-lo da frente da fila ({block_error}). O próximo "
                        "`queue` devolveria o mesmo item, e o run viraria um "
                        "laço nele — parar aqui é o menor dos dois estragos")
                    log_event({"evento": "esgotado", "id": ident, "tentativas": round_n,
                              "bloqueado": False, "erro": block_error})
                    break
                exhausted.append((ident, round_n))
                outcome(ident, "travado",
                         f"tirado da frente da fila (`blocked`) depois de "
                         f"{round_n} tentativa(s) sem sair do lugar"
                         + (f"; commits em `{side_branch}`" if side_branch else ""))
                log_event({"evento": "esgotado", "id": ident, "tentativas": round_n,
                          "bloqueado": True, "erro": None})
                step(f"{round_n} tentativa(s) sem progresso: marquei "
                      "`blocked` e a fila segue no próximo item")

            if consecutive_failures >= a.max_failures:
                end_reason = "disjuntor"
                end_detail = (f"{consecutive_failures} itens seguidos sem progresso — "
                               "isso é sistêmico, não azar; seguir queimaria a "
                               "janela no mesmo problema")
                break

    in_flight.clear()
    notify_hooks(ident if items else "a herança da largada")
    log_event({"evento": "run_end", "motivo": end_reason, "detalhe": end_detail,
              "itens": items, "com_progresso": len(done_items),
              "sem_progresso": len(failed), "esgotados": len(exhausted),
              "limite_de_uso": len(limited), "esperas_de_cota": len(waits),
              "quedas_de_rede": len(drops), "cota_apertada": len(tight),
              "entregues": len(delivered), "travados": len(blocked_items),
              "verify_vermelho": len(reds),
              "done_sem_commit": len(without_commit)})

    print()
    print(SCREEN.rule(f"fim às {datetime.now().strftime('%H:%M')} · {end_reason}"))
    print(f"   {end_detail}")
    if SCREEN.enabled:
        window_total = max((deadline - now).total_seconds(), 1)
        window_spent = (datetime.now() - now).total_seconds() / window_total
        print(SCREEN.c("cinza", "   janela ") + f"{now.strftime('%H:%M')} → "
              f"{deadline.strftime('%H:%M')}  " + SCREEN.bar(window_spent, 24)
              + SCREEN.c("cinza", f"  {min(window_spent, 1):.0%}"))
    paint = lambda n, color: SCREEN.c(color, str(n)) if n else str(n)  # noqa: E731
    print(f"   {items} tentativa(s) · {paint(len(delivered), 'verde')} entregue(s) · "
          f"{paint(len(blocked_items), 'vermelho')} travado(s) · "
          f"{paint(len(failed), 'vermelho')} sem progresso"
          + (f" · {len(limited)} interrompida(s) pelo teto de uso da conta"
             if limited else ""))
    if outcomes:
        print("\n   " + SCREEN.c("negrito", f"Itens ({len(outcomes)}):"))
        for ident, (kind, text) in outcomes.items():
            if SCREEN.enabled:
                glyph = OUTCOME_GLYPHS.get(kind, ("·", "cinza"))
                print("     " + SCREEN.c(glyph[1], glyph[0]) + " "
                      + SCREEN.c("negrito", ident) + SCREEN.c("cinza", f": {text}"))
            else:
                print(f"     - {ident}: {text}")
    if limited:
        print(f"\n   Teto de uso da conta ({len(limited)}) — não é falha "
              "do item:")
        for ident, reset in limited:
            print(f"     - {ident}: bateu o limite"
                  + (f", reseta {reset}" if reset else
                     " (o `claude` não disse quando reseta)"))
    if waits:
        print(f"\n   Esperas pela cota de 5h ({len(waits)}):")
        for when, ident, reset in waits:
            print(f"     - {when} ({ident}): esperei o reset das "
                  f"{reset.strftime('%H:%M')}")
    if tight:
        print(f"\n   Começados com a cota apertada ({len(tight)}) — o reset "
              "não cabia na janela, então segui em vez de parar:")
        for ident, usage, reset in tight:
            print(f"     - {ident}: cota em {usage:.0%}, reset às "
                  f"{reset.strftime('%H:%M')}")
    if drops:
        print(f"\n   Quedas de rede ({len(drops)}) — não é falha do item:")
        for ident, dropped_at, returned in drops:
            if returned is None:
                print(f"     - durante o {ident}: sem rede desde as "
                      f"{dropped_at.strftime('%H:%M')}, e ela não voltou a tempo")
                continue
            print(f"     - durante o {ident}: sem rede das "
                  f"{dropped_at.strftime('%H:%M')} às {returned.strftime('%H:%M')}, "
                  "depois retomei o item")
    cost = round(sum(costs.values()), 2)
    # The list of actions is closed (R2): after Revision 3 only
    # `aterrissar` remains. What no command executes goes to "fica com você".
    actions = []
    if close_empty_branch(repo, tree, start_branch, run_base):
        print(f"\n   branch da noite: nenhum commit — removi `{start_branch}` "
              "e a worktree dela")
    else:
        c, n = git(["rev-list", "--count", f"{run_base}..HEAD"], tree)
        n = n if c == 0 else "?"
        print("\n   branch da noite: " + SCREEN.c("ciano", f"`{start_branch}`")
              + f" ({n} commit(s) sobre a largada), em {short_path(tree, repo)}")
        actions.append(land_action(repo, tree, a.queue, run_id, n))
        for h in inheritance:
            print(f"   ela já contém `{h['branch']}` (herdada na largada): "
                  "mesclar a da noite leva as duas")
    stays = [{"id": ident, "texto": text}
            for ident, (kind, text) in outcomes.items()
            if kind in ("travado", "rota-humana", "done-sem-commit")]
    stays += [{"id": side, "texto": f"lateral não apagada, a cópia falhou: {error}"}
             for side, error in kept_side_branches]
    # Recomputed at the end, and not taken from `notified_hooks`: a warned hook
    # may have left the branch along with the red item that brought it.
    run_hooks = changed_hooks(tree, clone_base) if actions else []
    if run_hooks:
        stays.append({"id": "reinstalar-plugin", "texto": (
            f"a branch da noite muda {len(run_hooks)} hook(s) de plugin "
            f"({', '.join(run_hooks)}), e nenhuma rodada desta noite "
            "rodou com eles: os hooks vêm do plugin instalado. Passam a valer "
            "depois do `aterrissar` e de `bin/install.sh`")})
    if actions:
        print("\n   " + SCREEN.c("negrito", "Ações:"))
        for i, action in enumerate(actions, 1):
            print(f"     {i}. " + SCREEN.c("negrito", action['id']) + f": {action['frase']}")
            print(f"        como: " + SCREEN.c("ciano", action['comando']))
    if stays:
        # The items already have a line under "Itens"; here only the name, so the same item
        # doesn't show up as two problems (A4).
        of_items = [f_["id"] for f_ in stays if f_["id"] in outcomes]
        print("\n   " + SCREEN.c("negrito", f"Fica com você ({len(stays)}):"))
        if of_items:
            print(f"     {', '.join(of_items)} (a pergunta de cada um vem "
                  "no fim, em \"esperam por você\")")
        for f_ in stays:
            if f_["id"] not in outcomes:
                print(f"     - {f_['id']}: {f_['texto']}")
    save_state("esperando-dono" if actions or stays else "encerrado",
                 motivo_fim=end_reason,
                 itens=[{"id": i, "desfecho": t, "texto": x}
                        for i, (t, x) in outcomes.items()],
                 acoes=actions, fica_com_voce=stays,
                 custo_usd=cost if costs else None)
    # Final state recorded: a signal from here on (during the analysis) only ends the run,
    # without switching the state to `interrompido`.
    closed[0] = True
    if costs:
        br = lambda v: f"{v:.2f}".replace(".", ",")  # noqa: E731
        print(f"\n   custo: US$ {br(cost)} (soma do `total_cost_usd` de "
              f"{len(costs)} rodada(s): {' + '.join(br(v) for v in costs.values())})")
    print(SCREEN.c("cinza", f"\n   registro: {short_path(ledger, repo)}"))
    print(SCREEN.c("cinza", f"   saída do claude: {short_path(log, repo)}"))

    def ask_owner(review=None):
        # The summary above only counts; here each pending item becomes a question (09/30).
        try:
            item_states = json.loads(state_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            item_states = {}
        return close_with_owner(repo, a.queue, run_id, item_states, review,
                               wait=ANSWER_WAIT_SEC)

    # The analysis spends quota: stopping on the quota and then analyzing hits the
    # same ceiling. In those cases, and with nothing executed, it is left for by hand.
    if a.no_analysis or items == 0:
        return ask_owner()
    if end_reason == "limite-de-uso":
        print("   análise: não rodei (o run parou pela cota) — rode "
              f"`/common:until-review {short_path(ledger, repo)}` quando a cota "
              "voltar")
        log_event({"evento": "analise", "feita": False, "motivo": "cota"})
        return ask_owner()
    print("   análise: rodando /common:until-review…")
    review, review_error = analyze_run(repo, tree if tree.exists() else None,
                                      ledger, a.with_permissions)
    log_event({"evento": "analise", "feita": review is not None,
              "arquivo": str(review) if review else None, "erro": review_error})
    if review:
        print(f"   análise: {short_path(review, repo)}")
    else:
        print(f"   análise: falhou ({review_error}) — rode `/common:until-review "
              f"{short_path(ledger, repo)}` à mão")
    return ask_owner(review)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print("\ncepa-until: interrompido. O item em voo pode ter ficado "
              "reservado — o próximo `queue` o devolve como reserva órfã.",
              file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(130)
